verify_steps: (post-signup) GenerateGroupLink in own tenant → `mutation{guestAuthenticate(userId,companyId,roomId){user accessToken role}}` (no accessKey) vs POST /v2/auth/guest-link same triple → 200+token vs 401/422.
impact: accessKey-gated room entry bypass, cross-room guest impersonation; MEDIUM-HIGH.
testability: HUMAN_ONLY

**STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE**
- [PARKED] OIDC alg-confusion (ES/HS advertised, RSA-only JWKS): needs a token AND signing-key possession; subsumed by introspect finding, no independent lever.
- [FINAL] introspect (85) — survivors, sole non-zero delta this program's weeks; hinges on real-token test.
- [FINAL] IDOR (80) — highest impact, gated on tenant signup.
- [FINAL] guest-authz (60) — gated on tenant signup.

**STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION**
- [NEXT] HUMAN: Execute the standing signup plan — unauthenticated GraphQL `Signup`(planId "free-business") → email activation at `/finish-signup/{companyId}/{activationToken}` → POST /v2/auth/password {username,password} → opaque bearer → in ONE session: (a) GET /v2/users/me baseline then cross-tenant UUID probes (passcode → permissions → DELETE), (b) `mutation{guestAuthenticate(...){user accessToken role}}` real triple sans accessKey vs REST 3-field guest-link, (c) introspect any yielded token with fabricated `client_id` (Basic + POST-body). Also ask the client to launch the desktop app and capture which path `client-diagnostics-ingest.alfaview.com` POSTs to (ingest route discovery). Passive GET-only cycles are exhausted — every surface byte-stable.

**STEP 6 — LEARNING**
- [LEARN] NO_DELTA: all five live probes (OpenAPI MD5, users/me, OIDC discovery, authorize, graphql GET) byte-identical to prior cycle; introspect POST-channel idle per GET/HEAD/OPTIONS rule.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ sso.alfaview.com: OIDC discovery still advertises token_auth `[client_secret_basic, client_secret_post, none]` + ES/HS/RS id_token algs with RSA-only JWKS — listed, stable; no functional change.

**STEP 7 — RISK**
- [RISK] alfaview: 50/100 — unchanged. All probed surfaces byte-stable; no new anonymous exposure. Standing chains (introspect 85, IDOR 80, guest-authz 60) remain gated on tenant signup + token possession; score cannot move without a human clearing the signup gate.
