## STEP 6 — LEARNING

- [LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/token-info: first-ever mapping of a **fully unauthenticated** token-introspection endpoint on the production API, absent from 33 cycles of records. Documented 200 schema `TokenInfo{active, expiresAt, permissions}` is a validity-plus-permission oracle; two-tier 422 body (`"access token not in base64 format"` vs `"invalid access token format"`) is a confirmed format oracle; format gate is a structural binary parse (11-length base64 sweep all rejected); identical on `beta-apis`; query-param token supply is not distinguishable from the no-header case, so no token-in-URL claim is made.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED IDOR @ apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/group-link: the guest auth surface is **two** endpoints, not one — `/v2/auth/guest-link` and `/v2/auth/group-link` are distinct, and only the former is in the knowledge base. The unmapped one carries `externalId` ("used to derive a reproducible user ID", minLength 32), a caller-chosen identity-derivation input, and returns `participantId` plus a `clientLaunchUrl` embedding a live bearer in the `alfaview://` scheme. Spec-derived; not yet executed.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED AUTH @ apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/api-key: a third, never-mapped credential class (`{companyId, clientId, key}`) returning the same interchangeable `AccessToken` bearer as the password path, operator-provisioned via a support article, with a documented-but-never-observed account-status 403.
- [LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ tools.alfaview.com/whiteboard/*: the prior cycle's "second, previously-unmapped RPC backend" is an **empty service registration**, not a live data API. Proven by a `code:5` (no method in the table) vs `code:12` (method present, verb wrong) differential against the `/poll/` gateway, consistent across GET and OPTIONS and across 20 candidate service names. The mount is real; the service behind it is not callable.
- [LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json: the spec publishes **no `securitySchemes` and no per-operation `security`** across all 37 paths, while runtime enforcement demonstrably exists (`/v2/users/me` → 401/107B). API-hygiene/documentation defect that defeats automated auth-coverage tooling; informational, not independently reportable.
- [LEARN] NO_DELTA @ apis/sso/app/tools: OpenAPI MD5 `357b94d3` (127532B, 37 paths), JWKS 200/16257B (`3f8d456c`), OIDC 200/2169B, introspect OPTIONS 405, authorize 200/6176B, users/me 401/107B, graphql GET 400/406B, tools app-bundle md5 `b7f17c85` — all byte-identical; 33rd consecutive stable cycle. The cycle's entire yield came from reading the spec's previously-unexamined `/v2/auth/*` section, not from re-probing the standing surface.
- [RISK] alfaview: 61 — up from 59. The delta is a real, measured increase in *confirmed unauthenticated* surface on the highest-value asset: a production-API token-introspection endpoint that answers anonymous callers with differentiated structured errors and whose contract discloses token liveness plus a permission object. That matters beyond its own severity, because token liveness is the exact missing primitive gating every other HIGH-value chain in this program (poll BOLA, REST IDOR, SSO introspect) — each currently blocked only on possessing a valid bearer, and none able to check whether one still works. Bounded deliberately: no third-party credential was used, no customer or authentication data was read, no token was forged or cracked, every probe was a read-only GET/OPTIONS at ≤1 rps, and the two new POST endpoints remain unexecuted.
