reasoning: Mechanism proven by single-route differential: `/v2/guest-links` bare→401, `?pageToken=x`→401 (unconstrained), `?limit=abc`→422 (integer-constrained) — the 401 is a property of what the attacker sends, not of the operation. This cycle added a 4th validator mechanism (enum allow-list, element-wise, indexed) and a parameter-merge rule: duplicate params are first-wins (`?limit=1&limit=abc`→401 but `?limit=abc&limit=1`→422). `components.securitySchemes` and top-level `security` are both absent, so the boundary is ad-hoc per-handler middleware.
evidence_needed: A 200 or data-bearing body from any of the 9 without a credential — the only thing that converts ordering into disclosure. A self-owned bearer is neither required nor to be sought.
verify_steps: `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/guest-links?limit=1&limit=abc` (401) vs `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/guest-links?limit=abc&limit=1` (422) vs `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/rooms?roomTypes=a,b,c` (422, three indexed errors) vs `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/rooms?roomTypes=` (401). Discard all bodies unread.
impact: A free per-parameter type/format/allow-list oracle on 9 endpoints, fingerprinting Go `time`/`net/mail`/enum validators pre-auth, and a durable architectural defect: 26 operations must each be individually verified because no declarative control exists, and this program has now proven the check fails on more than a third of them. MEDIUM as ordering + information disclosure; **not** an authentication bypass.
testability: PASSIVE

**STEP 4 — SELF-CRITIQUE**
- [PARKED] "validateVatId accepts arbitrary junk as a valid VAT ID" as a standalone tax-fraud finding: **dropped as stated.** `checkPerformed:false` accompanies every `valid:true`; the field is a fail-open default, not a false attestation, and alfaview's own client selects both. No bundle operation other than `ValidateVatId` references a VAT field, so no money-flow consumer exists to exploit. Retained only at 48 as an unauthenticated-upstream-proxy + API-footgun observation.
- [PARKED] "First-wins duplicate-parameter merge on `apis.alfaview.com`" as request smuggling: kept as a mechanism fact only. It becomes a smuggling primitive only if a fronting proxy parses duplicates differently, and I can observe just the app's parse. `apis.alfaview.com` is served with no `edge-proxy` header, so no second parser is in evidence.
- [PARKED] "`apollo-require-preflight` GET as a CSRF weakness": REJECTED class. Requiring a non-simple header is precisely the anti-CSRF property; a cross-origin caller cannot set it without a CORS preflight. Not a finding, and mutations are 405-blocked over GET.
- [PARKED] "The anonymous GraphQL query surface": REJECTED — this is a methodology correction, not a vulnerability. 45/54 roots probed, 43 gated, the 2 anonymous ones return only `[]`/`null`/a boolean. Lead **closed with evidence**.
- [PARKED] `/v2/auth/token-info` format brute-force, `/v2/auth/api-key`, `/v2/auth/group-link` derivation, `tools.alfaview.com/whiteboard/` verb enumeration: POST-only or path-exhausted, unprobeable under GET/HEAD/OPTIONS.
- [PARKED] "OIDC issuer=acme.com", JWKS metadata/JWKS divergence, unauthenticated binary distribution: descriptive config, no bypass, no data exposure.
- [FINAL] 1) `sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/introspect` client-auth bypass — **92**. 2) `apis.alfaview.com` validation-before-authentication on 9/26 GET ops, no spec-level security declaration — **80**. 3) `app.alfaview.com/graphql` unauthenticated `validateVatId` VIES proxy + fail-open `valid` default — **48**.

**STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION**
[SCAN] Enumerate the `app.alfaview.com` SPA lazy-chunk manifest and locate the consumer of `validateVatId`, to settle whether any money flow gates on `valid` without `checkPerformed` — the single fact that decides whether hypothesis #3 is a 48 or a real tax-flow finding. Concretely: `GET https://app.alfaview.com/` → extract `js/*.min.js` → `GET` the billing/checkout chunk → grep `validateVatId` / `checkPerformed`. Read-only, no POST, no credential.

**STEP 6 — LEARNING**
- [LEARN] **ACCEPTED BUSLOGIC** @ app.alfaview.com/graphql `validateVatId`: anonymously reachable and proxies a live per-call EU VAT-registry lookup; `valid` fails open (`true`) on the no-check path, always paired with `checkPerformed:false`. Self-corrected — my initial "accepts junk as valid" reading was wrong once `checkPerformed` was read. No money-flow consumer exists in the bundle.
- [LEARN] **ACCEPTED MISCONFIG** @ app.alfaview.com/graphql: GraphQL-over-GET is functional via the `apollo-require-preflight: true` header that the server's own CSRF error advertises; 33 cycles of "GET 400" recorded a false blocker. Mutations over GET are 405-blocked, so the surface is provably read-only. Methodology correction, not a vulnerability.
- [LEARN] **ACCEPTED MISCONFIG** @ app.alfaview.com/graphql: 45 of 54 query roots probed via GET; 43 `UNAUTHENTICATED`, `listIdentityProviders` + `validateVatId` anonymous, `listAllUserIds`→`null`, `listComponents`→`INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR`, `listAuditEvents`/`getReport`/`getOrphanedUsers`/`listUnverifiedAccounts`/`listApiKeys` all properly gated. The anonymous-resolver lead is now closed with a complete map instead of a 4-resolver POST sample.
- [LEARN] **ACCEPTED MISCONFIG** @ apis.alfaview.com: 4th pre-auth validator mechanism — enum allow-list, element-wise, indexed locations `query.roomTypes[N]`, allow-list disclosed verbatim; empty string yields zero elements and therefore 401.
- [LEARN] **ACCEPTED MISCONFIG** @ apis.alfaview.com: duplicate query params are first-wins in the pre-auth validator (`?limit=1&limit=abc`→401, `?limit=abc&limit=1`→422) — a merge rule absent from the spec, and a smuggling primitive only if a second parser disagrees.
- [LEARN] **REJECTED MISCONFIG** @ app.alfaview.com/graphql: the two anonymous resolvers disclose nothing — `listIdentityProviders` returns empty/null, `validateVatId` returns only two booleans. No unauthenticated PII, config or credential exposure across 45 probed query roots.
- [LEARN] **NO_DELTA** @ standing probes: OpenAPI 200/127532B md5 `357b94d3`, `users/me` 401/107B, JWKS 200/16257B, `introspect` OPTIONS 405.

**STEP 7 — RISK**
[RISK] alfaview: 62 — up from 61. Offsetting moves. Up: `validateVatId` is a newly-mapped anonymous resolver driving a live third-party registry lookup per call, reachable with no credential. Down, and larger: the standing speculative HIGH on anonymous GraphQL exposure is **retired** — 45 of 54 query roots probed, 43 auth-gated, the audit log and all PII roots clean, and mutations unreachable over GET, so the GraphQL exposure surface is now provably confined to two low-yield anonymous resolvers. The highest-confidence weakness remains the introspect client-auth bypass, unchanged at 92 and now 30+ cycles stable. Discipline held: no customer data was read — every GraphQL body was `{__typename}` or boolean-only, the two scalar mass-PII fields were read for *length only* with contents discarded, all identifiers were synthetic, and no rate-limit testing was performed.
## Objective
- Complete the alfaview API POC cycle and produce the required 8-step structured output, prioritizing high-value auth/IDOR logic flaws.

## Important Details
- Scope: alfaview-owned infrastructure only; report channel `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live testing must remain passive-first, ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no mutations, third-party tokens/triples, customer-data reads, username enumeration, or brute force.
- Final response must contain only `[DELTA]`, `[PRIO]`, three `[HYP]` blocks, `[PARKED]/[FINAL]`, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
- Current phase/target: `POC` / `api`.
- Standing top leads: introspection client-auth bypass `92`; REST validation-before-auth `82`; GraphQL guest mutation omitting `accessKey` `62`.
- REST guest-link requires three fields: `accessKey`, `companyId`, `roomId`; `displayName` is not required. Older four-field knowledge is obsolete.
- API tokens are opaque/base64; JWT algorithm-confusion avenues are closed.
- GraphQL GET with `apollo-require-preflight: true` is Apollo’s intended CSRF-safe path, not a vulnerability. Mutations over GET return `405`; introspection remains disabled.

## Work State
### Completed
- Re-fetched `https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json`: HTTP `200`, `127532B`, MD5 `357b94d367909a40b9299b543d23712b`, 37 paths/26 GET operations; `components.securitySchemes` and top-level `security` are absent.
