class: MISCONFIG
asset: apis.alfaview.com/v2/users/invitation and /v2/users/invitations
confidence: 72
reasoning: HEAD/OPTIONS/GET on /v2/users/invitation returns 405/19B `text/plain` from `server: edge-proxy` with `allow: DELETE, POST`, while oa.json declares that path with methods=['post'] only. HEAD /v2/users/invitations (plural, not among the 37 spec paths) returns 405/19B with `allow: DELETE` and no other verb. Both bodies are `Method Not Allowed`; the unregistered control /v2/zzz-unregistered-control-9f3 is `404 page not found`, and declared app routes /v2/rooms and /v2/rooms/invitation are 401 application/problem+json — so the two invitation routes are served by a distinct Go router in front of the app, and 405 is emitted ahead of any 401. Beta is byte-identical, so one code path serves both environments. 14 sibling candidates (recordings, files, webhooks, api-keys, audit-log, permissions, companies, subscription, billing, users/invitation/accept) all returned 404, so the surface is exactly these two routes.
evidence_needed: One credential-free `DELETE /v2/users/invitations` returning anything other than 401/403 (202/204/404-by-id all count as reachable). A 401 closes the authorization question and leaves only the spec drift.
verify_steps: Read-only now — `HEAD https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/users/invitations` and `OPTIONS https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/users/invitation`, recording `allow:`; diff against the spec method list. Decisive step needs one self-owned invitation: DELETE with and without its own bearer.
impact: Unproven authorization-wise. If a DELETE is reachable pre-auth, any internet caller can revoke arbitrary tenants' pending user invitations — a cross-tenant onboarding-denial primitive, and a re-invite-to-attacker-email path if invitation state is consumed downstream. MEDIUM-HIGH if proven, currently zero. Independently and with certainty: the public contract understates the destructive surface, so integrators, scoped testers and WAF rules inherit a false map of a tenant-boundary resource. MEDIUM as spec integrity.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
