Closed the queued scan and found a new class. Evidence below, all read-only (9 GET/HEAD + 5 POST to auth-only paths, ≤1 rps, synthetic values only).

```
[NEW] apis.alfaview.com GET /v2/guest-links + GET /v2/group-links: the two company-wide link lists accept NO scoping parameter — only pageToken + limit. Room-scoped siblings exist separately (/v2/rooms/{roomId}/guest-links). The unscoped list is therefore a strict superset with no narrowing parameter, and GuestLink.required = [id, roomId, createdBy, createdAt, permissionGroupId, accessKey, emailAddress, locale, origin, dialInAllowed, dialInCode, joinUrl] — accessKey, joinUrl, dialInCode and guest emailAddress are all required members of every listed object.
[NEW] apis.alfaview.com TokenUserPermissions is a CLOSED vocabulary: additionalProperties:false, all 7 fields required = manageCompany, roomAdmin, roomCreate, roomList, userAdmin, userList, userShow. There is no guest-link or group-link axis. InviteUserPermissions is the identical 7-field set. The platform's own convention is that a company-wide list gets a named permission (roomList="list all rooms in their company", userList="list all users in their company") — the guest-link list is the one company-wide read whose sensitivity exceeds any published permission, and GET /v2/guest-links nevertheless declares 403 "The requesting user does not have the necessary permissions" while GET /v2/group-links does not.
[NEW] apis.alfaview.com RoomPermissions proves guest links ARE permission-bearing principals: guestLinkPermissions[] and groupLinkPermissions[] of ParticipantPermissions{participantId, permissions}; Permissions/Edit are a closed 9-field room-scope set where admin="...edit or delete rooms, change room settings or features and manage guests in the room". So guest-link management is room-scoped and permissioned by design, yet the company-scope token vocabulary has no axis for it at all.
[NEW] apis.alfaview.com POST /v2/auth/group-link is LIVE and unprobed in 34 cycles: HEAD → 405 `allow: POST`, text/plain, edge-proxy. The 2026-09-26 standing-probe list recorded it as 404 (that was a GET on a POST-only path). Redemption is documented to return an accessToken when the key is currently valid: GroupLinkAuthenticationInfo/GuestLinkAuthenticationInfo require [validFrom, validUntil, displayName] and add accessToken/clientLaunchUrl/participantId/tokenExpiresAt/webclientLaunchUrl, each documented "Can be empty if the ... link is not yet / no longer valid".
