[PARKED] accessKey existence oracle at /v2/auth/guest-link and /v2/auth/group-link: withdrawn by my own probe and retired as REJECTED. Both endpoints return a single post-lookup tier (422/88B ACTION_INVALID) for malformed keys, synthetic keys and a traversal string alike, so validity is not probeable; the brute-force and rate-limit framing that accompanied it is an out-of-scope enforcement-policy class.
[PARKED] externalId uniqueness delegation on POST /v2/auth/group-link (confidence 45): the schema states the caller "is responsible for providing a unique value per user" and the reply exposes participantId, so a server-side identity collision is possible, but impact depends entirely on client behaviour I cannot observe and no verify step exists that avoids entering a live customer room. No verify path, so it cannot be carried.
[PARKED] Silent privilege-tier change via GuestLinkUpdate.permissionGroupId with sendEmail:false (confidence 44): the minimum payload is displayName plus sendEmail and the update also carries emailAddress, validFrom/validUntil, so an authorization tier can be changed with the guest notification suppressed. Blocked because it is the write half of H1's identical chain and needs the same read access; splitting it would double-count one asset. Folded into H1 as impact.
[FINAL] H1 apis.alfaview.com company-wide un-narrowable guest-link credential list with no expressible authorization primitive — 71 (new class, both halves provable from the published contract with no credential, resolution AUTH_HELPED on one self-issued token)
[FINAL] H2 app.alfaview.com adminSwitchCompany cross-tenant admin token mint — 55 (signature, argument name and a valid internal tenant ID all public; anonymous reachability untested)
[FINAL] H3 sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/introspect unenforced client authentication — 94 (standing, passively re-confirmed, no regression)
```

```
[NEXT] PROBE (AUTH_HELPED, read-only, one self-owned account): (1) GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/token-info with `Authorization: Bearer <self-issued token>` and record the `permissions` object verbatim — this single read decides the entire core of H1, since a closed 7-field token vocabulary means the company-wide credential list has no expressible gate. (2) If and only if step 1 returns only the 7 documented fields, GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/guest-links?limit=1 and record status and content-length only, never the body. (3) If step 2 is 200, GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/guest-links?limit=500&roomId=<a room id the same account owns> and compare content-length against step 2: a smaller body proves a hidden scope filter and downgrades H1 to a documentation gap, an equal body proves there is no narrowing path at all. No PATCH, no guest-link redemption, no third-party tenant. The human gate is account creation itself, which is where this chain stops being mine to run — an email-verified self-owned account plus its own guest link is the entire prerequisite.
```

```
[RISK] alfaview: 68 — held flat, deliberately. This round produced no exposure: 8 GETs, all 401/107B, no 200, no response body reflecting input, no data. But it also produced a structural result worth more than a null: the authenticated surface is provably uninspectable from outside, because the edge proxy rejects before query and path validation, so the last credential-free angle on H1 is closed by measurement rather than by patience, and I have stopped proposing new passive angles for it. Two signals pull in opposite directions and roughly cancel. Negative for risk: the gateway is uniform and hygienic — one 107-byte static 401 across all 37 paths, no tenant or parameter reflection, no divergence between malformed and well-formed input, no vendor headers, and every credential-free avenue I tried this cycle came back empty; there is no low-hanging unauthenticated surface on this API and the risk that an obvious one exists has fallen. Positive for risk: the finding now rests entirely on a contract reading that cannot be corroborated without a credential, and its severity is high enough that the program's next meaningful step is human, not automated — the chain is a single self-issued token from a room access credential the product hands out as a share link. Discipline held: 8 requests at ~1.3s, GET only, no credential, no account, synthetic zero UUIDs and the string abc, no guest, user, room or tenant data read, and the two spec inspections were local file reads. I am explicitly retiring a five-cycle lead of my own (the accessKey existence oracle) and explicitly correcting a method error of my own from the prior turn (a discriminator that the architecture made impossible), because both would otherwise have consumed budget indefinitely while looking like progress.
