[PARKED] Pre-auth query-parameter binder as a standalone enumeration oracle: **downgraded to informational, by my own pre-registered closure condition.** I wrote that a complete sweep whose recognized set matches the contract on every route "would close it as 'the binder exposes the published schema'". That condition is now met — three per-operation negative controls, ten candidate filters all negative, and every disclosed value (`<= 50`, `<= 500`, required-ness, the `department/room/meeting` enum, the Go time layout, the RFC-5322 email check) equal to the published contract. It reproduces `/v2/docs/openapi.json` and nothing more. Demoted rather than dropped, because it is still the instrument that closed H1's scope half, and that credit belongs in H1's evidence.

[PARKED] Two-tier 401 and the false `"No base64 encoded access token"` message: rejected class (descriptive errors only) and zero attacker value — the tier is keyed on whether the client sent a header, which the client already knows. Its one residual use is stated inside H3 as the control that closes the token-validity-oracle question; it is not promoted to a finding.

