impact: An unauthenticated caller can enumerate the entire route table, and via the `Allow:` header the method table, of a multi-tenant video-conference API whose entire authenticated surface returns a single indistinguishable 401 by design. No data is exposed and no authentication is bypassed, so this is an information-disclosure and control-bypass-in-depth finding rather than a direct compromise; it is the reconnaissance primitive that makes every other chain in this program cheaper, and it is what would let an attacker find an undeclared destructive method without ever holding a token. LOW standalone / MEDIUM as an enabler, and the reportable core is "authentication is enforced after routing and method dispatch", not "404 pages are verbose".
