impact: Any party can ask the IdP whether an arbitrary token is live and receive back its full claim set, so token validity and contents are confirmable without client credentials. This does not by itself yield a token and is capped by the program's own note on authentication data; the reportable core is the missing client authentication on a token-introspection endpoint, not token theft. HIGH severity for a production IdP, zero impact without a token to introspect.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

