- **[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com:** authentication is enforced *after* routing and method dispatch, so the entire route table and method table of a multi-tenant video API is enumerable by an unauthenticated caller. Three pre-auth terminal states, each distinguished by status, content-type **and** body md5: `401`/107B/`application/problem+json`/`60ed2f29` (registered, app runtime), `405`/19B/`text/plain`/`34c520d8` + `Allow:` (registered, Go runtime, wrong method), `404`/19B/`text/plain`/`595e8801` (unregistered). Proven with four negative controls and two positive controls, at 1 rps, with no credential and no customer data. This extends the already-measured validation-before-authentication ordering on 9 of 26 GET ops to the routing layer itself, and it is the one place in this program where the discriminator is a **branch** rather than a message — so it is not the program-rejected descriptive-error class. Scoped honestly: no data disclosed, no authentication bypassed, LOW-MEDIUM standalone, and its value is that it is the reconnaissance instrument whose yield is exactly the set of routes the published `openapi.json` omits, which is how the undeclared `DELETE /v2/users/invitations` was originally found.
- **[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com — my own claim from two consecutive cycles, retracted and replaced:** "the authenticated API handles any path with one uniform 401" (then narrowed to "uniform per header-presence state") is **wrong about the mechanism**. `GET /v2/zzznotreal` returns `404`, not `401`, so the router discriminates registered from unregistered before authentication. The cause is identical to the retraction I filed last cycle and worth naming as a pattern: in both cases I generalised from a set with **no negative control in the branch I was describing** — last cycle a positive control for a recognized parameter, this cycle any probe of an *unregistered* path. Two cycles of notes asserting "no new endpoints" rested on a control I never ran. The corrected rule is that uniformity holds only across the set of registered paths, and my standing `NO_DELTA`/`no new endpoints` language should be read as "no change among routes I happened to probe" until the oracle sweep above has been run over the namespace.
