## Objective
- Continue POC-phase bug-bounty analysis of `apis.alfaview.com`, identify the current OpenAPI surface delta, prioritize new anomalies, and produce the required structured hypothesis output.

## Important Details
- Scope: alfaview company-owned infrastructure and `alfaview.com` subdomains; report channel `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live probes must remain passive-first, `<=1 rps`, and GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; do not POST, mutate data, enumerate real users/tenants, or expose authentication/customer data.
- Prior `[NEXT]` for `POST https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/api-key` with `{}` is blocked by the current GET/HEAD/OPTIONS-only rule.
- Final response must contain only the requested structured blocks: `[DELTA]`, `[PRIO]`, up to three strict-schema `[HYP]` blocks, `[PARKED]`/`[FINAL]`, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
- Standing high-value chains: SSO introspection client-auth bypass `94`; guest-link credential list/IDOR `80`; API-key taxonomy `52`; pre-auth route/method enumeration `63`.
- Current repository commit: `ac3716b`.

