`[PARKED]` `participantId` polymorphism on `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` — parked on **measured counter-evidence, not on effort**. `participantId` accepts a guest-link or group-link ID while only `{roomId}` appears in the path, and identifiers for all three principal types come from company-wide un-narrowable lists, so this looked strong mid-cycle. But the same route declares a **409** its PATCH sibling does not — the first 409 in the contract — and 409 on a write is the conventional code for a state conflict, which is what a failed participant↔room binding check would produce. The cross-company variant needs two tenants, a worse blocker than the one I already have. Revisit only if a token-gated 403 is observed.

