## STEP 1 — DELTA

`[NEW]` **`GET /v2/group-links` (`ListGroupLinks`) declares no `403`; `GET /v2/guest-links` (`ListGuestLinks`) does.** Controlled pair — identical parameters (`Authorization`, `pageToken`, `limit`), identical `PaginatedBodyList*` pagination wrapper, and both payloads require `accessKey`, `joinUrl`, `dialInCode`, `roomId`, `id`. The *only* difference across the whole contract is the declared 403. This inverts the standing finding: the guest-link list at 80 is the **gated** half, not the ungated one.

`[NEW]` **`POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` is `CreatePermissions`** — "Creates permissions for a user that are applied in a room" — body `ParticipantPermissions`, whose `permissions` is `Permissions` with **all 9 booleans required including `admin`**. A create can therefore mint an explicit `admin: true` record for any `participantId`. The 409 description is **"The resource already exists."** (duplicate-create guard), and its 404 is **"Room was not found."** — the room is the only resource the create path names. The PATCH sibling's 404 says "Room **or user permission** was not found." There is no PATCH on the collection path; the PATCH is on `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}`, a different resource.

`[NEW]` **`GET /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` (`ListPermissions`) declares no `403`**, while all three writes on that same resource do. Returns `RoomPermissions` = `userPermissions[]`, `guestLinkPermissions[]`, `groupLinkPermissions[]`.

`[NEW]` `PATCH` body `PermissionsEdit` is the same 9 axes but **all nullable, none required** — PATCH is partial, POST is full replacement. `promote` is documented "for other users", which is what makes the self-grant variant interesting.

`[NEW]` **Base rate for 403-absence: 14 of 27 GETs declare no `403`.** Absence alone is the majority convention here and proves nothing.

`[CHANGED]` `app.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json` → `302 Found. Redirecting to /` → SPA shell `200`. Priority-5 target from last cycle, never tested, now closed negative: there is no second API surface on the app host, and the 37-path baseline is not recoverable there.

`[CHANGED]` `account_creation: restricted — only on test/sandbox assets` (scope.yml:44). My previous `[NEXT] HUMAN` assumed a live company signup was mine to request. It is not, without program blessing.

