## STEP 1 — DELTA

**[NEW] `apis.alfaview.com` contract contains ZERO `pattern:` constraints.** Enumerated every `components.schemas` property and every parameter object across all 38 paths / 57 operations: not one `pattern` keyword exists anywhere. First measurement of the contract's input-constraint surface in 36 cycles.

**[NEW] RETRACTION of my own 2026-09-03→2026-09-29 standing claim.** The assertion "OpenAPI spec confirms path-param UUID patterns for permission and user delete" is **false**. `id`, `roomId`, `userId`, `subroomId` are each declared exactly `{"type":"string"}` — no `format: uuid`, no `pattern`, no minLength/maxLength. The only UUID-shaped artifact is a cosmetic `examples: ["00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"]` on `GuestLink.id` / `GuestLink.roomId`. I read an example as a constraint.

**[NEW] `apis.alfaview.com` — the two sole guest-admission bearer credentials are declared with no entropy contract at all.** `GuestLink.accessKey` ("The access key.") and `GuestLink.dialInCode` ("The dial-in authentication code.") are both `{"type":"string"}` — no format, no pattern, no length bounds — while both are in `required`. `GuestLinkCreate` carries `dialInAllowed` but **not** `dialInCode`, so both are server-generated. `GroupLink` mirrors this exactly.

**[NEW] `companyId` is a ULID.** The production tenant ID hardcoded in the public app bundle (`01FDY0986YK1BJF2K0F9DXR8EB`, md5-verified source) is valid Crockford base32; its 48-bit timestamp prefix decodes to **2021-08-25T06:34:43.294Z**. The contract's own example `"0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP"` is **not** a well-formed ULID — it contains `I`, `L`, `O`, which Crockford excludes. Identifier generation is time-ordered; the published example does not instantiate the format the vendor's own client ships.

**[NEW] Credential-transport isolation, measured (7 controlled requests).** `Authorization` / `authorization` / `AUTHORIZATION` all reach the identical 122B md5 `3d0dc74b` base64 tier → header matching is **case-insensitive** (no WAF/case differential). No-header, `token:`, `Grpc-Metadata-alfaview.token:` and `x-access-token:` all reach the identical 107B md5 `60ed2f29` "No access token was provided" tier → the REST API honours **no** credential transport but `Authorization`. The app GraphQL `token` header and the in-room poll `Grpc-Metadata-alfaview.token` header are **not** interchangeable with the REST bearer.

**[NEW] `/v2/auth/*` family is contract-clean.** OPTIONS on all five returns `405/19B` with `Allow` exactly matching the declared method set (`api-key|group-link|guest-link|password` → `POST`; `token-info` → `GET, HEAD`). The program's one confirmed `Allow:`-vs-spec divergence (`/v2/users/invitation` = `[DELETE, POST]` vs spec `[POST]`) is confirmed still **isolated**, now across the whole auth family.

