## STEP 6 — LEARNING

**[LEARN] REJECTED AUTH @ apis.alfaview.com (credential-transport confusion, class closed):** Seven controlled requests on `/v2/users/me` establish that header-name matching is case-insensitive and that `Authorization` is the *only* honoured credential transport. `Authorization`/`authorization`/`AUTHORIZATION` are indistinguishable (401/122B md5 `3d0dc74b`, "No base64 encoded access token…"), while absent-header, `token:`, `Grpc-Metadata-alfaview.token:` and `x-access-token:` are indistinguishable from each other (401/107B md5 `60ed2f29`, "No access token was provided in the Authorization header."). Two consequences, one negative and one positive. Negative: there is no WAF/case differential to exploit, and the app GraphQL transport and the in-room poll transport are **not** interchangeable with the REST bearer — the three surfaces have genuinely separate credential paths. Positive: the error text is a *reliable* signal that the header was parsed at all, which is a cheaper discriminator than the byte length I retracted as unstable two cycles ago.

**[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com/v2/users/invitation (upgrade condition still unmet):** OPTIONS on all five `/v2/auth/*` routes returns 405/19B `text/plain` behind `edge-proxy` with `Allow` exactly matching the declared method set — `api-key`, `group-link`, `guest-link`, `password` → `[POST]`; `token-info` → `[GET, HEAD]`. The single undeclared-destructive-method divergence found on 2026-09-27 remains isolated across the whole auth family, so the 63-confidence route-enumeration branch stays parked. Recording the negative so the branch is not silently revived.

**[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com (contract, evidence-integrity):** The 38-path / 57-operation contract contains **zero** `pattern` keywords, and `id`, `roomId`, `userId`, `subroomId` are declared bare `{"type":"string"}`. This voids my own 26-cycle-old claim that the spec "confirms path-param UUID patterns" — the only UUID artifact is a cosmetic `examples` entry on `GuestLink.id`/`roomId`. Recorded as ACCEPTED because the measured fact stands on its own: the platform publishes no input contract for the identifiers consumed by its own unscoped destructive operations.

**[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com (credential contract):** `accessKey` and `dialInCode` are declared `{"type":"string"}` with no format, pattern or length bounds, while both are `required` on `GuestLink` and `GroupLink` and both are server-generated (`*Create` accepts `dialInAllowed` but not `dialInCode`). No entropy floor is published for either guest-admission credential. No REST-side attack path claimed — there is no dial-in endpoint in the contract.

**[LEARN] ACCEPTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com/v2/users/me/company (identifier scheme):** `companyId` is a 26-character ULID. The production ID in the public bundle, `01FDY0986YK1BJF2K0F9DXR8EB`, is valid Crockford base32 with a 48-bit prefix decoding to 2021-08-25T06:34:43.294Z. The contract's own example, `"0123456789ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOP"`, is a sequential counter and is *not* a well-formed ULID (`I`, `L`, `O` are excluded from Crockford). Time-ordered, so any disclosed companyId discloses tenant creation time; enumeration is explicitly **not** enabled, since 80 of 128 bits remain random.

**[LEARN] NO_DELTA @ sso/apis/tools:** 35th+ consecutive byte-stable cycle. OpenAPI md5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2` (132100B, 38 paths, 57 ops) on both prod and beta; OIDC 200/2169B md5 `f78a08fc` with `introspection_endpoint` absent while `/oauth2/introspect` stays live at OPTIONS 405; JWKS 200/16257B md5 `3f8d456c` with 7 RSA/RS256 keys against 9 advertised algs including the symmetric and ECDSA families; tools `/whiteboard/` 404/47B and poll `list` 501/55B unchanged. No new endpoints, no regressions, no new unauthenticated exploit surface.

## STEP 7 — RISK

**[RISK] alfaview: 57** — Unauthenticated attack surface is effectively nil after 36 cycles: every probe returns 401, 405, 404 or a pre-auth 422 that reproduces the public specification and nothing beyond it (the binder oracle was already downgraded to informational on that basis). The risk sits entirely in two places, both unproven on the wire. The high end is a real control-plane gap set with a documented redemption chain: an un-narrowable company-wide guest-link list returning `accessKey` + `joinUrl` + telephony `dialInCode` + guest `emailAddress`, redeemable unauthenticated, with no expressible permission able to gate it, and a public bundle that discloses a cross-tenant admin-token-minting signature. The 94-confidence item — `/oauth2/introspect` accepting a fabricated `client_id` on both POST-body and Basic with no runtime secret verification, while `/oauth2/userinfo` in the same FusionAuth 1.63.0 build tiers correctly against forged JOSE — is a proven missing check whose impact is capped by the program's authentication-data exclusion and which needs a valid token to matter. Every chain above the informational tier is gated on one absent account, and this cycle established the cost of the decisive test is now exactly three read-only GETs. Score held flat rather than raised: nothing was demonstrated this cycle, and one of my own long-standing supporting claims was withdrawn.
