STEP 1 — DELTA (amendment, same cycle)

[NEW] alfaview supports BRING-YOUR-OWN-IdP single sign-on, documented at
support.alfaview.com/en/for-it-administration/integrations/single-sign-on/ — "use your existing identity provider to log
in to alfaview", requiring OpenID Connect or SAML V2.0, with GitLab (OIDC), Google Workspace (SAML V2.0) and Shibboleth
(SAML V2.0) listed as proven-compatible. Each SSO company gets its own alfaview-hosted login domain (e.g.
my-company.alfaview.com), and the security guide confirms SSO joins occur "through an alfaview subdomain" with a
distinct web address structure. The doc also provides "Manage groups for single sign-on authentication users" and a
"user group attribute... for group based permission management in alfaview" — establishing SSO users as a population
ALONGSIDE native alfaview users.

[NEW] Every alfaview user is provisioned with a NATIVE password independent of any IdP.
administration/user-management/invite-user/ (200/82KB): "The contained link must be opened in the browser in order to
activate the user account and set a password. Users can only be invited or created by email. It is not possible to
specify a user with a predefined password." There is no SSO scoping on this flow, no documented way to create a
passwordless/IdP-only user, and no article in the KB describing how to disable local password authentication or enforce
SSO-only login.

[NEW] The SSO article's own "Limitations" section addresses only SAML signature algorithm and IdP-initiated flow
("We do not support identity provider initiated SAML V2.0"), and is silent on local-account coexistence.

[NEW] alfaview's security-guide (200/105KB) lists "Activate the two-factor authentication" as a personal self-service
security tip — a per-user toggle, not a company-enforced policy — and the 2FA article scopes it to "alfaview version
9.2.0 or higher" desktop. So 2FA is a user hardening control in the vendor's own framing, and the documented mechanism
for company-wide auth control is the customer IdP, not 2FA.

[NEW] NEGATIVE RESULT — v1 API is gone. https://apis.alfaview.com/v1/docs/openapi.json and .../openapi/openapi both
404/19B despite the KB stating "Version 1 ... will be discontinued in March 2027". No unmapped deprecated surface.

[NEW] NEGATIVE RESULT — the OpenAPI 3.0.3 twin is semantically IDENTICAL to the 3.1 original. 132391B md5 34e9f231,
same 38 paths, same 57 operations, zero path differences, "two-factor" x2 in both, byte-identical password description
