performs no federation check. (1) alfaview documents BYO-IdP SSO with per-company login subdomains, and separately
documents "Manage groups for single sign-on authentication users" — proving two user populations coexist: federated and
native. (2) The user-invite flow sets a native password for every user: "The contained link must be opened in the browser
in order to activate the user account and set a password", with no SSO scoping and no passwordless option. (3)
POST /v2/auth/password is globally unauthenticated — one of only five unauthenticated endpoints in the entire 57-op
