## Objective
- Continue the alfaview gmbh POC (`phase: POC`, `target: api`) and finish the required structured DELTA→RISK analysis.
- Assess anonymous GraphQL query reachability using GET-only requests, then report only evidence-backed findings.

## Important Details
- Stay passive-first: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 request/second, no mutations or auth-bypass testing against live data.
- Do not retrieve or expose customer/employee/authentication data; stop/redact if a query unexpectedly returns sensitive values.
- Final response must contain only the prescribed `[DELTA]`, `[PRIO]`, `[HYP]`, `[PARKED]/[FINAL]`, one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]` blocks.
- Keep facts separate from hypotheses; drop confidence `<40`, rejected classes, or hypotheses without concrete verification.
- `access-control-allow-origin: *` exists without `access-control-allow-credentials`; do not report wildcard CORS alone as exploitable.
- Current API baseline: OpenAPI 38 paths/57 operations; `/v2/users/me/company` is the sole 200-response supplier of `companyId`.
- High-value account-gated chains remain unresolved: guest-link enumeration, destructive IDOR/BOLA, GraphQL admin operations, SSO/native-password 2FA asymmetry.

## Work State
### Completed
- Verified `https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json` and beta twin: HTTP 200, 132100 bytes, MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`.
- Verified OIDC discovery: HTTP 200/2169, MD5 `f78a08fced8b042093396383b74d8458`, issuer `acme.com`.
- Verified JWKS: HTTP 200/16257, MD5 `3f8d456c7fd92c6107f3fd77732bd0f4`, 7 keys.
- Verified standing controls unchanged: `/oauth2/introspect` OPTIONS 405; `/v2/users/me` 401/107, MD5 `60ed2f29d492ec872c598cc7d36aa37e`.
- Plain `GET https://app.alfaview.com/graphql?query={__typename}` returns HTTP 400/406 with Apollo CSRF guidance naming `x-apollo-operation-name` or `apollo-require-preflight`.
- `GET https://app.alfaview.com/graphql?query={__typename}` with `x-apollo-operation-name: probe` returns HTTP 200/32: `{"data":{"__typename":"Query"}}`; GET-only GraphQL execution is confirmed.
- Current bundle `https://app.alfaview.com/js/app.min.67e8a68d4318b34ca241.js` returns 1092529 bytes, MD5 `2cb9128353b1f7444e222b4b61e4ffa5`; old `app.min.5b3949112f0cf682adc8.js` redirects to `/`.
- Bundle extraction recovered 58 query and 90 mutation operation names. High-value query targets include `ListAllUserIds`, `ListAllUserProfiles`, `ListUsersByIds`, `ListApiKeys`, `ListAuditEvents`, `ListAuthData`, `ListCompaniesById`, `ListRoomGuestLinks`, `FetchSSOInfo`, and `GetBillingInfo`.
- Recovered exact documents include `query ListAllUserIds { listAllUserIds }`, `query ListAllUserProfiles { listAllUserProfiles { users } }`, `query GetOrphanedUsers { getOrphanedUsers { userProfilesWithNoAuth orphanedUserAccounts } }`, and `query FetchUserPermissions($userId: String!) { fetchUserPermissions(userId: $userId) { permissions } }`.

### Active
- Extracting exact GraphQL documents, arguments, and reply fields for the high-value queries; prior broad extraction was truncated around `ListApiKeys`.
- Preparing safe anonymous GET auth-gating probes, prioritizing non-sensitive fields or synthetic identifiers before any potentially credential-bearing query.
- Delta so far: standing API/SSO probes show NO_DELTA; GET-capable GraphQL query execution is a newly confirmed surface capability, not yet a vulnerability.

### Blocked
- Anonymous behavior and authorization enforcement for the remaining GraphQL queries are not yet measured.
- Exact query signatures for several high-value operations still need targeted extraction from the bundle.
- Mutations cannot be executed under the current read-only rules, even if GraphQL accepts them over GET.
- Fully authenticated IDOR, 2FA, signup-email, and tenant-isolation tests still require a self-owned account/tenant.

## Next Move
1. Run targeted extraction against `/tmp/opencode/r39/app.js` for exact documents and return types of `ListApiKeys`, `ListAuditEvents`, `ListAuthData`, `ListCompaniesById`, `ListRoomGuestLinks`, `FetchSSOInfo`, and `GetBillingInfo`.
2. Probe safe read-only queries anonymously with `curl -G --data-urlencode 'query=...' -H 'x-apollo-operation-name: probe'`, spaced ≥1 second; request only `__typename` or synthetic-ID inputs where possible and stop before any sensitive-data response.

## Relevant Files
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/app.js`: current 1.09 MB public GraphQL/admin bundle; source of all operation signatures.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/apis.alfaview.com_v2_docs_openapi.json`: production OpenAPI snapshot.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/beta-apis.alfaview.com_v2_docs_openapi.json`: byte-identical beta OpenAPI snapshot.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/oidc.json`: OIDC discovery evidence.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/jwks.json`: seven-key JWKS snapshot.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/me.json`: unauthenticated `/v2/users/me` response.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/h3.txt`: headers proving GET GraphQL execution with `x-apollo-operation-name`.
- `/tmp/opencode/r39/g3.txt`: successful `{ "__typename": "Query" }` response body.
