  resource ID, and free-form before/after action diffs — and those user UUIDs are precisely the missing input
  to DELETE /v2/users/{id} and PATCH /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}, the two unscoped destructive
  operations this program has carried as its standing IDOR target with no way to supply an identifier since
  2026-09-03. Severity HIGH if confirmed. NOT claimed: no wire evidence of an authorization defect.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
```

```
[HYP] Token introspection client authentication is absent in the same FusionAuth build that validates
      tokens correctly on userinfo
class: MISCONFIG
asset: sso.alfaview.com POST /oauth2/introspect
confidence: 94  (unchanged — CARRIED, not re-measured this cycle)
reasoning: Carried verbatim from the 2026-09-27 cycle, which strengthened it with a same-deployment
  control: /oauth2/userinfo correctly tiers and rejects forged JOSE in the identical FusionAuth 1.63.0
  build, so introspect's missing client check is an omission, not an architectural choice. Discovery still
  advertises token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported = [client_secret_basic, client_secret_post, none].
  I fired no POST this cycle, so this number is not a fresh measurement.
evidence_needed: A valid, legitimately-issued access token, then introspection via a fabricated client_id
  and a fabricated secret, to show whether a token is described to an unauthenticated caller.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED, one self-owned token. `POST /oauth2/introspect` with the real token in the body
  and `client_id`/`client_secret` both fabricated. Compare against the same request with the correct
  client_id. Divergence in the `active`/claim set is the finding.
impact: MEDIUM. Disclosure of token validity and claims to an unauthenticated caller; no token forgery
  follows, because issuance is still gated. Confidence is high on the mechanism, unmeasured on the impact.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
```

```
[HYP] The company-wide group-link list is documented asymmetrically against its guest-link twin, so a
      client cannot tell whether an authorization tier exists
class: MISCONFIG
asset: apis.alfaview.com GET /v2/group-links (ListGroupLinks) vs GET /v2/guest-links (ListGuestLinks)
confidence: 55  (unchanged — CARRIED, not re-measured this cycle)
reasoning: Unchanged. Measured this cycle that the full 57-op response-code map still shows
  ListGuestLinks declaring {200,401,403} where ListGroupLinks declares only {200,401} — and I re-confirmed
  the 403-declaration table is not behaviourally load-bearing, because /v2/permission-groups declares no
  401 yet returns 401/107B. So the divergence is a contract defect, not evidence of a missing check.
evidence_needed: A low-privilege self-issued token on a self-owned tenant, GET /v2/auth/token-info to record
  the `permissions` bits verbatim, then GET /v2/group-links?limit=1 recording the status code.
verify_steps: AUTH_HELPED, read-only. `GET /v2/auth/token-info`, then `GET /v2/group-links?limit=1` with
  that token on the same self-owned tenant, recording status and whether group-link credentials return.
impact: LOW, API-contract defect. Explicitly NOT a claim that authorization is missing.
testability: AUTH_HELPED
```

