## STEP 6 — LEARNING

```
[LEARN] ACCEPTED IDOR @ apis.alfaview.com GET /v2/audit-log: a live, undocumented 39th path, absent from
  the 38-path contract and from the entire 37-cycle recon snapshot, is the operation described by four
  schema definitions that no operation references (Event, Actor, Target, PaginatedBodyListEvent — the
  last referenced zero times). Its pre-auth binder is complete and negative-controlled: from/to required
  date-time, limit 1..50, actionType enum read|write; pageToken, outcome, actorType, targetType and sort
  do not bind. Valid parameters return 401/107B, so the gate holds and no data was read. The payload
  carries actor.userId with a support|async_task actor enum, targets[].id, free-form details, and stored
  checksums — a company-wide source of exactly the user UUIDs this program has lacked since 2026-09-03 for
  DELETE /v2/users/{id} and PATCH /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}. TokenUserPermissions has no
  audit axis and the contract contains no audit parameter at all. Auth gate measured, authorization
  behaviour unmeasured; AUTH_HELPED.
[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com: the pre-auth 422 on /v2/audit-log is not itself a finding.
  It reproduces schema constraints that are publishable in principle, carries no data, and was already
  downgraded to informational on 2026-09-28. Used here only as the measuring instrument for the binder map.
[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com: "/v2/audit-log is undocumented, therefore it is a weakness"
  is the class I rejected on 2026-09-27 for tools.alfaview.com/whiteboard/ and it is rejected again. Absence
  from a published contract is not absence of a control; the 401/107B on valid parameters is positive
  evidence that one is present.
[LEARN] REJECTED SURFACE @ apis.alfaview.com: /v2/audit-log/{uuid} and /v2/audit-log/{metadata,
  metadata-attributes, searchable-metadata, attributes} all 404/19B. No detail route, no metadata-attribute
  route under this prefix. The Event.metadata description's named operation remains unlocated.
[LEARN] METHOD: an orphan-schema diff is a cheap, zero-request route-discovery primitive. Computing
  components.schemas minus the transitive reference closure of paths yielded 7 orphans; 5 (ErrorModel,
  ErrorDetail, RoomQuotas) resolved as benign on inspection, but 4 unused schemas formed a coherent,
  fully-described API that the route table did not contain. It took one 9-second HEAD sweep to confirm the
  route was live. This is worth repeating on every contract rotation — the 37→38 delta I identified last
  cycle by path-set diff would have surfaced nothing here.
```

## STEP 7 — RISK

```
[RISK] alfaview gmbh: 72. Raised from 68 on one newly discovered live route, not on any confirmed weakness.
  The trigger is: an endpoint the vendor ships the full response schema for but does not publish, reachable
  pre-authentication for validation, replicating on beta byte-for-byte, whose payload yields a
  company-wide time-ranged enumeration of internal user UUIDs, alfaview support-staff actor IDs and every
  affected resource ID — and for which the complete published contract contains no permission, no parameter
  and no endpoint able to express an authorization check. The auth gate itself measured correct (401 on
  valid parameters, zero data read), and the whole surface is otherwise byte-stable for a 35th consecutive
  cycle, so the score reflects an unmeasured high-class lead rather than a demonstrated defect. The
  escalation trigger remains one authenticated read on a self-owned tenant.
```
## Objective
- Continue the alfaview bug-bounty POC analysis, investigate the latest OpenAPI anomalies, and return the user’s required structured analyst blocks.
- Current focus: determine whether orphan audit/event schemas expose an undeclared or unmapped endpoint.

## Important Details
- Phase/target: `POC`, `api`; report channel: `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Scope: alfaview-owned infrastructure and subdomains only.
- Final response must contain only structured blocks: `[DELTA]`, `[PRIO]`, `[HYP]`, `[PARKED]/[FINAL]`, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, `[RISK]`.
- Keep facts separate from hypotheses; do not claim authorization defects without wire evidence.
- Live testing is passive-first, `<=1 rps`, and limited to `GET/HEAD/OPTIONS`; no mutations, credential attempts, or customer-data access.
- Current standing evidence:
  - `https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json`: HTTP 200, `132100B`, MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`, 38 paths, 57 operations.
  - `https://sso.alfaview.com/.well-known/openid-configuration`: HTTP 200, `2169B`, MD5 `f78a08fced8b042093396383b74d8458`.
  - `https://sso.alfaview.com/.well-known/jwks.json`: HTTP 200, `16257B`, MD5 `3f8d456c7fd92c6107f3fd77732bd0f4`.
- Current OpenAPI has no `components.securitySchemes` and no top-level `security`.
- Leading authenticated hypotheses remain:
  - Company-wide `GET /v2/guest-links` and `GET /v2/group-links` expose live credentials with no scope filter or expressible guest-link permission.
  - `sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/introspect` accepts fabricated clients but impact requires a valid token.
  - Native-password/API authentication may coexist with SSO despite customer-enforced IdP 2FA.
- High-value live verification is blocked by the lack of a self-owned authenticated account; GraphQL signup is email-gated and `HUMAN_ONLY`.

