## Objective
- Continue the alfaview bug-bounty PoC cycle for `apis.alfaview.com`, compare current surface, rank hypotheses, and output the required seven structured blocks.
- Highest-value authorization tests remain blocked on one human-owned low-privilege account and self-owned tenant data.

## Important Details
- Scope: alfaview company-owned infrastructure only.
- Passive-first, `<=1 rps`, live probes limited to GET/HEAD/OPTIONS; no customer-data exposure or out-of-scope testing.
- Rejected classes must not be resurrected: brute force, username/accessKey enumeration, descriptive errors alone, JWT confusion, SSRF, mass assignment, clickjacking without impact, and scanner-only claims.
- Signup is anonymous but email-gated: `app.alfaview.com/graphql` `Signup` → email → `FinishSignup`; therefore `HUMAN_ONLY`.
- Current risk score: `62`.
- Closed/falsified avenues: no guest/group-link `accessKey` oracle, no REST SSRF primitive, no profile mass assignment, no API/SSO JWT algorithm confusion, no logout open redirect.
- Final output must contain exactly one `[NEXT]` action.

## Work State
### Completed
- Current OpenAPI is prod/beta byte-identical: HTTP 200, `132100B`, MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`, `38 paths`.
- `/v2/users/me/company` is the identified 38th path and supplies the caller’s own `companyId`.
- Live undocumented `/v2/audit-log` remains validation-before-auth:
  - Bare GET → `422/232B`, MD5 prefix `b4adcd15`, errors for `query.from` and `query.to`.
  - Valid `from`/`to` → `401/107B`, MD5 prefix `60ed2f29`.
- Standing probes were stable:
  - `/v2/users/me`, `/v2/users/me/company`, `/v2/room-types` → `401/107B`, MD5 `60ed2f29`.
  - OIDC → `200/2169B`, MD5 `f78a08fc`.
  - JWKS → `200/16257B`, MD5 `3f8d456c`.
  - `/oauth2/introspect` OPTIONS → `405`.
  - `tools.alfaview.com/whiteboard/` → `404/47B`.
  - `tools.alfaview.com/poll/pollservice/list` → `501/55B`.
  - `client-diagnostics-ingest.alfaview.com/health` → `200 {"status":"ok"}`.
  - `app.alfaview.com` shell → `200/1381B`.
  - `test.alfaview.com` still distributes alfacheck `483102` for four platforms.
- CORS sweep found only `app.alfaview.com/graphql` with `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`; no `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials`. OPTIONS allows `content-type,token`. This is informational, not exploitable credentialed CORS.
- Authorization-header controls were stable:
  - Missing/empty header → `401/107B`, MD5 `60ed2f29`.
  - Any nonempty Bearer, case variants, or duplicate headers → `401/122B`, MD5 `3d0dc74b`.
  - `X-Forwarded-Host`, `X-Original-URL`, and `X-Real-IP` spoofing did not bypass auth.
- New query-parameter probes on `/v2/room-types`, participants, permissions, and permission-groups all remained uniformly auth-bound.
- Guessed high-value subdomains such as `admin.alfaview.com`, `auth.alfaview.com`, `git.alfaview.com`, and `vault.alfaview.com` returned `000`.

### Active
- Finalize the seven-block cycle from existing evidence; no further network request is currently necessary.
- Leading hypotheses:
  1. `sso.alfaview.com POST /oauth2/introspect` lacks client authentication — confidence `94`, blocked on a real token.
  2. `GET /v2/guest-links` + `GET /v2/group-links` may expose credential-bearing company-wide records — confidence `90`, blocked on a low-privilege token.
  3. `GET/POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` may allow a member to read peers and mint room-admin rights — confidence `62`, entirely behaviorally unmeasured.

### Blocked
- No self-owned low-privilege account or bearer token is available.
- No self-owned tenant `roomId` for a room the account has merely joined.
- Therefore introspection claim disclosure, link-list authorization, and room-permission escalation remain unmeasured.

