## STEP 1 — DELTA SUMMARY

**[NEW] One previously unrecorded unauthenticated surface: the Stoplight docs UI.**
- `GET /v2/docs/openapi` → `200`, `1214B`, `text/html`. It is a Stoplight Elements shell whose `apiDescriptionUrl` is `/v2/docs/openapi.yaml`. No auth, no customer data.
- `GET /v2/docs/openapi.yaml` → `200`, `165360B`, md5 prefix `6738669c`. This is a **YAML twin** of the JSON spec, distinct from the previously recorded 3.0.3/3.1 twins.
- Parity: `beta-apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi` → `200/1214B`, identical.

**Set-level comparison (JSON vs new YAML), measured not assumed:**
- JSON: 38 paths / 57 ops. YAML: 38 paths / 57 ops.
- Path sets are **exactly equal** in both directions (0 only-in-YAML, 0 only-in-JSON).
- `securitySchemes` count `0` and `security:` count `0` in the YAML; JSON `components` contains only `schemas`, top-level `security` absent. Spec-debt confirmed across a second rendering, so it is no longer a JSON-parser artifact.

**Sharpened, not new — H3 (room permissions).** The new YAML lets me read the vendor's own permission vocabulary rather than infer it. `Permissions` exposes nine required booleans including `promote` ("Permission to promote permissions for other users") and `admin` ("allowed to edit or delete rooms, change room settings or features and manage guests"). `ParticipantPermissions.participantId` is documented as "The user ID / **guest link ID / group link ID** to which the permissions apply" — one endpoint governs three distinct principal types. Net effect: the tenant-scoping intent for `CreatePermissions` is explicit, so the cross-tenant *write* escalation weakens; the *read* enumeration and the `promote`-gate question become the sharper target. Corroborated by vendor KB `room-permissions` (200, `89064B`): permission groups Admin/Moderator/Participant/Guest/Spectator/No-access.

**Sharpened, not new — audit-log.** Full binder sweep on the undocumented route establishes the complete parameter set is `from`, `to`, `limit` only. There is **no** client-supplied tenant or actor filter, so tenant isolation on `/v2/audit-log` is entirely server-side.

**Four avenues closed this cycle (all measured, all negative):**

| Probe | Result |
|---|---|
| Host-header injection across `app`, `tools`, `sso`, `alfaview.com/en` | `Host: evil.example.com` → `421` at the edge; `X-Forwarded-Host` ignored; 0 occurrences of `evil.example.com` in any body |
| `ACAO: *` on `app.alfaview.com/graphql` vs cookie-based session | No `set-cookie` on app root or graphql; auth is header-borne. `access-control-allow-credentials` absent. **Not exploitable** |
| `/v2/docs/*` sibling renderings | `docs/`, `docs/index.html`, `docs/openapi/3.0.3`, `docs/openapi/3.1`, `swagger.json`, `redoc` all `404/19B` |
| Stoplight static assets | `av-footer.js` `200/1714B`, `design_tokens_light.css` `200/25964B`, `web-components.min.js` served, `operations_sorter.js` `404` — no leak, only one `00000000-...` placeholder UUID in the whole spec |

## STEP 2 — NEW FINDINGS

No new reportable finding. Nothing this cycle clears the bar: the YAML twin is semantically identical to the JSON already under assessment, the docs UI exposes nothing the JSON does not, and every auth/authz behavior probe returned a pre-auth or spec-level result.

One item worth recording as a hypothesis input rather than a finding: `GET /finish-signup?activationToken=…&companyId=…&username=…` returns `302/23B` (an unauthenticated URL-borne activation credential). The 302 target is sanitized, so referer/log leakage is unproven and untestable without a real token from a real activation email.

## STEP 3 — KNOWLEDGE BASE UPDATES

**Assets.** `beta-apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi` recorded as byte-identical to prod for the docs UI.

**Endpoints added.**
- `GET /v2/docs/openapi` — `200`, `1214B`, `text/html`, md5 prefix `0de38500`, unauthenticated.
- `GET /v2/docs/openapi.yaml` — `200`, `165360B`, md5 prefix `6738669c`, unauthenticated, spec debt.

**Schema.** `Permissions`: nine required booleans, notably `promote` and `admin`. `ParticipantPermissions.participantId` is a union key across users, guest links, and group links. `PermissionsEdit` is the partial-update form. `PermissionGroup` carries `id`/`name`/`permissions`.

**Spec debt.** Unauthenticated public spec and docs UI declare **no** security scheme for a 57-operation API where every `users/me`, `room`, and `guest-links` operation requires a bearer token. Audience is a third party: developers generate real credentials against this document. Now confirmed on two independent renderings.

**Hypotheses.**
- H-AUDIT-LOG: no client-side narrowing exists, so the tenant filter is server-side only. Prediction unchanged (predicted false, `AUDIT_LOG` bit 21), blocked on a token.
