## Objective
- Continue the alfaview gmbh POC against `apis.alfaview.com`, prioritizing proven or testable IDOR/auth/SSRF/GraphQL/OAuth logic flaws.
- Deliver the required eight-step, structured bounty analysis without inventing findings or touching customer data.

## Important Details
- State: `phase=POC`, `target=api`.
- Scope: alfaview-owned infrastructure, APIs, web/desktop/mobile apps, support systems, portals, websites, and `alfaview.com` subdomains.
- Live testing: passive-first, `<=1 rps`, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only; no mutations, auth bypass, customer/employee data access, brute force, descriptive-only issues, scanner-only claims, or out-of-scope classes.
- Required final structure: `[DELTA]`, `[PRIORITIZE]`, exactly three `[HYP]` blocks, `[PARKED]`/`[FINAL]`, exactly one `[NEXT]`, `[LEARN]`, and `[RISK]`.
- Facts and hypotheses must remain separate; each hypothesis needs exact asset, confidence, evidence, concrete requests, impact, and testability.
- Current standing leads:
  - Confidence 94: `sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/introspect` accepts fabricated `client_id` via POST-body and HTTP Basic; real-token impact remains unmeasured.
  - Confidence 90: unscoped `GET /v2/guest-links` and `GET /v2/group-links` expose join credentials with no expressible link-specific authorization axis; token-gated.
  - Confidence 62: `GET/POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` may permit low-privilege room-admin escalation; entirely unmeasured.
- Current OpenAPI: 38 paths, 57 operations, 132100 bytes, MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`; prod and beta are identical.
- `/v2/audit-log` is an additional live undocumented path, making 39 observed REST paths.
- OpenAPI has `top-level security=None` and no `components.securitySchemes`; authentication is handler/edge middleware rather than declarative.
- New route-oracle claim is not yet complete: samples prove registration/GET support classification, but `Allow:` discloses other methods only when GET produces 405.

