## [DELTA]

Cycle 40 is a **negative-result cycle plus one new mapping fact**. The substantive change is that the route/method oracle is no longer a hypothesis — it is a proven, app-wide instrument, and it has been used to close three previously-open branches with measurements.

**New surface found (never probed in 39 prior cycles):**
- `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/docs` → **200**, `text/html`, 843B, `server: edge-proxy`. A **Stoplight Elements 9.0.15** API-reference UI, titled `alfaview Reference`.
- CSP is strict and correct: `default-src 'none'; connect-src 'self'; script-src` limited to a single SRI-pinned `unpkg.com/@stoplight/elements@9.0.15` URL, with `sandbox allow-same-origin allow-scripts allow-popups`.
- `GET /v2/docs/openapi` → 200, 1214B, a **second, self-hosted** Stoplight variant (`hideSchemas="true"`, scripts at `/docs/stoplight/web-components.min.js` 2083393B, `/av-footer.js` 1714B, `/v2/docs/operations_sorter.js` 303B). Both variants point at the same `apiDescriptionUrl`.
- This disclosed the **canonical spec URL that all prior work had missed**: `/v2/docs/openapi.yaml`.

**The spec-variant class is now closed definitively.** `GET /v2/docs/openapi.yaml` → 200, **165360B**, `application/openapi+yaml`, md5 `6738669c92a893c56e157c3927044134`. Full structural diff vs. the JSON twin: **38 paths / 57 operations / 38 schemas on both**, zero paths, operations or schemas unique to either side, `securitySchemes` **ABSENT in both**, top-level `security: null` in both, identical `servers`, and a description-level diff of **935/935 nodes, 56222/56222 characters** with **57/57** `x-sort-index` extensions matched. Zero `example` nodes in either rendering, so no identifier- or credential-like values leak. Byte-size difference (165360 vs 132100) is pure YAML verbosity, not extra content. This is the third rendering tested (`/v2/docs/openapi.json`, `/v2/docs/openapi` 3.0.3, `/v2/docs/openapi.yaml`); all three are semantically identical.

**The pre-auth route/method oracle is proven and generalized.** Four-state control matrix, all reproduced this cycle:
- absent route → `404` / 19B / `text/plain` / `404 page not found`
- registered, GET-declared → `401` / 107B / `application/problem+json` / `www-authenticate: AccessToken`
- registered, GET-not-declared → `405` / 19B / `text/plain` / **`Allow:` disclosing the live method set**
- registered, GET-declared, unauthenticated validation tier → `422` / 141B with `{"title":"Unprocessable Entity","detail":"validation failed","errors":[{...}]}`

**`Allow:` is behaviourally load-bearing — a 9/10 exact match against the declared spec.** Live reads on all declared-no-GET paths: `/v2/auth/api-key`→`POST`, `/v2/auth/group-link`→`POST`, `/v2/auth/guest-link`→`POST`, `/v2/auth/password`→`POST`, `/v2/meetings/{id}/cancellation`→`POST`, `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/guest-links/{id}`→`DELETE`, `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/group-links/{id}`→`DELETE`, `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}`→`DELETE, PATCH`, `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/subrooms/{subroomId}`→`DELETE, PATCH`. Exactly **one** divergence: `/v2/users/invitation` declares `POST` but serves **`Allow: DELETE, POST`**.

**The REST surface is closed.** **32/32** undocumented route candidates returned `404` (17 flat nouns incl. `/v2/companies`, `/v2/tenants`, `/v2/api-keys`, `/v2/webhooks`, `/v2/integrations`, `/v2/recordings`, `/v2/subrooms`, `/v2/permissions`, `/v2/audit-events`, `/v2/metrics`; 10 room sub-resources incl. `members`, `guests`, `users`, `recordings`, `stats`, `polls`, `whiteboard`, `chat`; 4 meeting sub-resources; 9 `/v2/auth/*` incl. `token`, `refresh`, `logout`, `sso`, `oidc`, `signup`). Only `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/participants` (401) and `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/attendances` (422) are undocumented-but-live. Plus 10 unexamined prefixes all absent: `/v1`, `/v3`, `/internal`, `/admin`, `/api`, `/v2`, `/v2/`, `/openapi.json`, `/swagger.json`, `/health`, `/metrics`.

**One predicted-false chain is now measured rather than inferred.** `GET /v2/audit-log?from=2026-09-28T00:00:00Z&to=2026-09-30T00:00:00Z` → **401** / 107B / `application/problem+json` / md5 `60ed2f29d492ec872c598cc7d36aa37e`. The pre-auth `422` is purely the query binder: `limit=abc` still yields `422 invalid integer` at `query.limit`, while `companyId`, `userId` and `pageToken` are all unbound (`401`). The route binds **only** `from`/`to`/`limit` and takes no caller-supplied company selector — architecturally consistent with company-scoped, token-resolved design. The predicted-false call is correct.

**Reconfirmed:** `TokenUserPermissions` is a closed 7-field vocabulary (`manageCompany`, `roomAdmin`, `roomCreate`, `roomList`, `userAdmin`, `userList`, `userShow`), all 7 `required`, `additionalProperties: false` — third independent confirmation that no guest-link or group-link permission axis exists on the token object. `GuestLink` requires 12 of 15 fields including `accessKey`, `joinUrl`, `dialInCode`, `emailAddress`. `APICredentials` is `{companyId, clientId, key}`, all required.

## [PRIORITIZE]

The only pre-auth attack surface in the entire API is the four unauthenticated credential-exchange endpoints (`/v2/auth/password`, `/v2/auth/guest-link`, `/v2/auth/group-link`, `/v2/auth/api-key`). Everything else is `401`/`405`/`404`/`422`-bound. All three top hypotheses require a credential, so impact must be ranked first and feasibility second.

1. **SSO introspection missing client verification** — confidence 94, highest impact (token forgery for any client in the tenant), but impact is unmeasurable without a real token.
2. **Guest/group-link join-credential disclosure** — confidence 90, broadest blast radius (third-party join access to customer rooms), unmeasured.
3. **Room-permission self-escalation** — confidence 62, most feasible to prove (pure IDOR, single token, self-owned room), narrowest blast radius (own company only).
4. *New candidate, not promoted:* `POST /v2/auth/api-key` credential-validity oracle — see Parked.
5. *Closed this cycle:* undeclared-DELETE class, audit-log IDOR, spec-variant class, SSRF-to-metadata, IDN, GraphQL, OAuth, unauthenticated-read. All now measured negatives.

## [HYP]

**HYP 1 — SSO introspection accepts unauthenticated client verification, enabling cross-client token forgery.** Asset: `sso.alfaview.com` (`https://sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/introspect`, OIDC discovery 200/2169B, JWKS 200/16257B with seven RS256 keys). Confidence **94** that client authentication is not verified; impact confidence materially lower. Evidence: historical probing confirmed the endpoint accepts fabricated `client_id` via both POST-body and HTTP Basic; OIDC discovery 200/2169B, JWKS 200/16257B with seven RS256 keys, no `client_secret` in any public source. The introspection response is the sole decision point for whether a JWT is accepted downstream. Verify: one POST with a real self-owned token, varying only the `client_id` across the user's own clients, comparing `active` and error fields. Impact if real: mint or replay tokens for any client in the tenant, unauthenticated. Testability: **token-gated and one-shot** — introspection normally consumes the token, so a single live token cannot be safely replayed; the test must be a batch in one authenticated session. Do not fire new POSTs in the current passive budget.

**HYP 2 — Unscoped guest-link and group-link listing discloses third-party join credentials.** Assets: `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/guest-links`, `GET /v2/group-links`, `GET /v2/rooms/{roomId}/guest-links`, `GET /v2/rooms/{roomId}/group-links`, `POST /v2/auth/guest-link`, `POST /v2/auth/group-link`. Confidence **90**. Evidence: `GET /v2/guest-links?limit=abc` → 422/141B proves the route is live and binds pre-auth; `GuestLink` requires `accessKey`, `joinUrl`, `dialInCode`, `emailAddress` (12 of 15 required); `TokenUserPermissions` has **no guest-link or group-link axis** (confirmed three times, closed 7-field `additionalProperties: false` schema). The vulnerability is therefore not a missing permission flag but an **absent link-scoped authorization axis**: no expressible selector in the token model distinguishes which links a caller may read. Verify: one low-priv token, two self-owned rooms, `GET /v2/guest-links` and `GET /v2/group-links` unpaginated. Impact if real: read every guest and group link in the tenant including `accessKey`, `joinUrl`, `dialInCode` and target `emailAddress` — unauthorized third-party join to customer meetings. Testability: **token-gated, single request, high signal-to-noise** — the cleanest test in the portfolio.

**HYP 3 — Low-privilege room-admin escalation via `PATCH /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}`.** Assets: `GET/POST https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions`, `PATCH/DELETE /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}`. Confidence **62**. Evidence: spec declares **no company selector** on the whole family — only the path-bound `roomId` — so the only possible scoping is room membership; live `Allow: DELETE, PATCH` confirms the write exists and matches spec; `TokenUserPermissions.roomAdmin` is a coarse boolean with no per-user granularity; `RoomPermissions` carries `userPermissions`, `groupLinkPermissions`, `guestLinkPermissions` groups, implying per-user control. The escalation is that `roomAdmin=true` may permit granting `roomAdmin` to oneself. Verify: one token with `roomAdmin=false` on a room it merely joined, one `PATCH` setting its own `userId` to `roomAdmin=true`, then one `GET /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions`. Impact if real: self-escalation to room administrator. Testability: **token-gated but the most feasible** — pure IDOR, single token, self-owned room, one mutating call.

## [PARKED]

- **New, parked below the top three — `POST /v2/auth/api-key` credential-validity oracle.** `/v2/auth/api-key` is the **only** one of the four unauthenticated credential-exchange endpoints that declares a `403` tier ("e.g., account is inactive"); the other three declare only 400/401. `APICredentials` is `{companyId, clientId, key}` with `clientId` described as "the alias of the API key", and `companyId` is the input to every sibling endpoint. If a 403 or status/latency split separates unknown-`clientId` from known-client/wrong-key, that yields valid company/client credential enumeration — the prerequisite for the entire guest-link chain. Confidence ~25, and the honest caveat is decisive: **declared codes are not behaviourally load-bearing**, proven twice today (`GET /v2/users/{id}/permissions` returns 401 while declaring no 401; `/v2/permission-groups` declares no 401 and returns 401). The 403 tier is a weak signal, not evidence. Parked because it still needs an account to mint a self-owned API key.
- **`/v2/users/invitation` undeclared `DELETE`** — now **measured as a genuine single instance**, 1/10 against a 9/10 exact-match baseline. No second instance exists. Retire.
- **`/v2/audit-log` IDOR** — **retired by measurement**: valid params → 401, and the route binds no company selector. Predicted-false confirmed.
- **Spec-variant class** — **retired**: three renderings, all semantically identical at description level.
- **`/docs` Stoplight UI** — **mapped, non-finding.** The public reference was already public via `/v2/docs/openapi.json`; the CDN variant is SRI-pinned and CSP-sandboxed, the self-hosted variant serves only same-origin assets, and no credential, token or internal endpoint appears in either. Informational at most; the program rejects descriptive-only findings.
- **Still token-gated:** SSO (94), guest/group-link (90), room-permission (62). Account creation via `app.alfaview.com/graphql` `Signup` → email → `FinishSignup` remains email-gated and HUMAN_ONLY. Required state: company `roomCreate+roomList`, `roomAdmin=false`, plus a merely-joined self-owned `roomId`, and one real self-owned token.

## [FINAL]

Recon is **complete and closed at the unauthenticated tier.** 39 REST paths confirmed (38 documented + `/v2/audit-log`), 3 semantically identical spec renderings, 3 interactive UIs, and a proven pre-auth route+method oracle. **Zero unauthenticated data access.** No new reportable vulnerability was found this cycle; the cycle's value is one new mapping fact (`/docs` → canonical `/v2/docs/openapi.yaml`), three branches retired by measurement instead of inference, and the removal of a speculative 14-candidate route sweep in favour of an exhaustive 32-candidate one.

## [NEXT]

Request from the reporter one low-privilege self-owned alfaview account plus one real self-owned access token: company-level `roomCreate` + `roomList`, `roomAdmin=false`, and the `roomId` of one room the account has merely joined — the exact state already specified in the standing account-creation task. That single credential unblocks all three hypotheses at once and is the only thing gating further progress.

## [LEARN]

- A **pre-auth three-state oracle** (`404` absent / `401` registered+auth-gated / `405` registered+GET-disallowed) makes exhaustive route enumeration reliable on this API, and the `405` state's `Allow:` header discloses the live method set, turning a documentation-inference class into a measurable one. This is the single highest-leverage technique developed in 40 cycles and it should be the default tool for any future Go-mux/FastAPI-style target.
- **Documentation renderings are not interchangeable evidence.** The JSON spec that 39 cycles relied on was not the canonical rendering; the vendor's own UI loads `/v2/docs/openapi.yaml`. Always enumerate the docs directory and read the UI's `apiDescriptionUrl` before treating a spec as complete.
- **Always follow the HTML.** A single 843-byte unauthenticated page at `/docs` disclosed a 165KB never-fetched artifact that 39 cycles of direct API probing had missed. Cheap unauthenticated HTML is often the highest-yield recon per request.
- **Probe documented-no-GET paths with GET.** It is the cheapest possible method-enumeration primitive, requires no mutation, and yields the live `Allow:` set for free. Nine of ten matched the spec exactly, which retroactively validates using the spec as a baseline at all.
- **Two probe shapes must be distinguished.** Pre-auth `422` is the query-parameter binder; pre-auth `401` is the authorization gate. Attributing a `422` to an authorization question produces false leads — as the `audit-log` case nearly did.
- **A "single known instance" is only single after you find the denominator.** 19 candidates in earlier cycles implied uniqueness; the 9/10 denominator made it measurable and closed the branch.
- **Negative results are results.** Three branches closed this cycle were each previously carried as open, and each was consuming reasoning budget in every subsequent cycle.

## [RISK]

- **Credential-safety.** `/v2/auth/guest-link`, `/v2/auth/group-link` and `/v2/auth/api-key` are unauthenticated credential-exchange endpoints. Any testing beyond the documented schema risks minting valid join credentials. No POST has been fired this cycle; all requests were GET.
- **Token consumption.** SSO introspection is typically one-shot per token, so a careless probe can destroy the only credential available. This is why the introspect test must be batched in one authenticated session.
- **Mutating surface.** `PATCH/DELETE /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}` and the guest/group-link `DELETE` family are destructive and unscoped by company. One stray write to a foreign `roomId` is a real customer-impacting incident. Everything this cycle was read-only and pre-auth.
- **Data handling.** If HYP 2 confirms, the response bodies contain live customer `emailAddress` values and join credentials. Treat as customer data: self-owned rows only, redact, do not retain.
- **Third-party script execution.** `/docs` executes `unpkg.com` JavaScript on the `apis.alfaview.com` origin. It is SRI-pinned and CSP-sandboxed so the current risk is low, but it is a third-party dependency on an API origin and any SRI or CSP regression there would be directly exploitable. Worth one line in the report as an observation; not a finding.
- **Account creation.** `FinishSignup` is email-gated. Do not attempt to bypass the gate; the account task stays HUMAN_ONLY.
- **Rate and scope discipline.** Every request this cycle was a single unauthenticated GET at ≤1 rps with a browser UA, against `apis.alfaview.com` only, with no attempt at customer or third-party tenant hosts.
