## Objective
- Run a passive-first alfaview API delta hunt in `POC` phase, validate standing anomalies, then emit the requested structured `[DELTA]` through `[RISK]` blocks.
- Prioritize high-value IDOR/BOLA and auth/business-logic chains without inventing runtime findings.

## Important Details
- Scope: company-owned alfaview infrastructure only; report channel `bugs.olivermaicher.eu`.
- Live-probe rules: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps, no mutation/auth bypass, no customer-data exposure.
- Exclude rejected classes: brute-force/rate limits, descriptive errors, scanner-only output, known-library findings, clickjacking without exploit, public login panels, etc.
- Separate measured facts from hypotheses; provide exact HTTP requests and one concrete `[NEXT]` action.
- Highest-value standing lead remains authorization on `GET /v2/guest-links` and `GET /v2/group-links`; runtime behavior requires a self-owned low-privilege token.
- `/v2/rooms/{id}/participants` may supply internal `userId` UUIDs but remains auth-gated.
- `tools.alfaview.com/whiteboard/` is an unmapped RPC prefix with no demonstrated exploit.

