## [STATE]
Cycle 36, `POC` phase. 43 requests, all GET/HEAD, ≤1 rps, no credentials, no mutation. Scope: `*.alfaview.com`.

## [DELTA]
**6 new facts, all on `apis.alfaview.com` unless noted.**

1. **`GET /v2/docs/changelog` → `200`/4338B/md5 `90948aa4`, prod==beta byte-identical.** Never recorded in the corpus. Linked only from `/`, not from the `/v2/docs/openapi` UI. Content is security-relevant (see [FINDINGS] 1).
2. **`GET /v2/docs/openapi` → `200`/1214B/md5 `0de38500`, prod==beta byte-identical.** A second HTML entry point to the same spec that had never been probed in 36 cycles. Distinct from the recorded `/docs` (843B/md5 `66404dd6`): different Stoplight build, self-hosted rather than `unpkg.com`-pinned, and a weaker CSP.
3. **`GET /v2/docs/operations_sorter.js` → `200`/303B.** The relative `src` in `/v2/docs/openapi` resolves to `/v2/docs/…`, not `/docs/…` — my first attempt at the absolute path 404'd. Its entire body is a comparator on `extensions['x-sort-index']`, which mechanically explains the `x-sort-index` holes (24, 25, 26, 30, 31) recorded as REJECTED on 2026-09-29: they are reserved sort slots, not removed endpoints.
4. **`GET /v2/docs/openapi-3.0.json` → `200`/132391B/md5 `34e9f231`; `…-3.0.yaml` → `200`/161928B/md5 `29aed8d2`**, prod==beta. These are the exact URLs of the "3.0.3 twin" recorded without locations on 2026-09-29. Re-verified: same 38 paths, `securitySchemes` absent and top-level `security` absent in *both* renderings, per-operation `security` identical.
5. **CSP is inconsistent across the three HTML entry points on one origin.** Measured:

| path | CSP |
|---|---|
| `/docs` | `default-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; connect-src 'self'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; sandbox allow-same-origin allow-scripts allow-popups allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox; script-src https://unpkg.com/@stoplight/elements@9.0.15/…` |
| `/v2/docs/openapi` | `default-src 'self'` **only** — no `frame-ancestors`, no `base-uri`, no `sandbox` |
| `/` and `/v2/docs/changelog` | **no CSP header at all** |

`X-Frame-Options` absent everywhere (already on record for all hosts).
6. **`GET /v2/room-types` → `401`/107B/md5 `60ed2f29`** on prod *and* beta. First measurement of this route in 36 cycles. With `?limit=abc`, `?name=abc`, `?used=abc` → byte-identical `401`. It declares **zero query parameters**, so it is the one GET operation where the pre-auth binder oracle provably cannot exist.

**Standing reconfirmations (no delta):** OpenAPI `284a3383`/132100B/38 paths/57 ops, `securitySchemes` absent; OIDC `f78a08fc`/200/2169B; JWKS `3f8d456c`/200/16257B; `tools…/whiteboard/` 404/47B; `GET /v2/users/invitations` 405 `allow: DELETE` (Go router); `GET /v2/audit-log` bare → 422/232B naming `query.from` + `query.to`, and with valid `from`/`to` → 401/107B.

**Closure of two parked items:** transitive orphan-schema diff (not just direct `$ref`) yields true orphans `{Actor, Event, Target, PaginatedBodyListEvent, ErrorModel, ErrorDetail}` — the audit family plus the RFC 7807 wrappers. `/v2/audit-log` is therefore the *sole* live consumer of that family, and this primitive can derive no further undocumented REST route. Separately, the changelog independently corroborates that the 37→38 path delta measured on 2026-09-28 was `GetOwnCompany`, dated `28.09.2026` in the same release as the spec md5 move.

## [PRIO]
1. **2FA bypass via API-key authentication** — vendor-confirmed in their own changelog, unauthenticated to establish, and it disarms a control the same platform enforces elsewhere.
2. **Guest/group-link company-wide list** — standing H1, unchanged, still the highest-impact chain if a token arrives.
3. **Participant-identity read** — standing H2, supplies the UUIDs that H1's destructive siblings need.

## [FINDINGS]
1. **ACCEPTED · AUTH · confidence 82** — `apis.alfaview.com` documents a method-dependent 2FA downgrade in its public changelog. Verbatim: *"14.04.2026 — Allowed users with two-factor authentication enabled to authenticate via an API key (second factor not required then)"*. The asymmetry is structural, not incidental: `POST /v2/auth/password` enforces 2FA (the `17.03.2026` entry records `500 → 403` for that case, and the `28.09.2026` entry records a bug where 2FA password auth returned an empty token instead of `403` — i.e. the vendor actively maintains a 403 tier for it), while `POST /v2/auth/api-key` does not, keyed on **which credential is presented** rather than on the account's 2FA policy. API keys are the long-lived per-company trust class (`APICredentials` = `clientId` + `companyId` + `key`, all required, `additionalProperties:false`). An operator who enables 2FA to contain a compromised *password* has not contained a compromised *API key*, and nothing in the response distinguishes a session that skipped the second factor. **Zero wire evidence claimed** — the API-key POST was never fired; this rests on the vendor's own published statement plus the contract. Related corroboration in the same document: `26.05.2026` *"Improved security by omitting request details in error responses"*, a hardening pass that left the residual pre-auth 422 field-name disclosure intact.
2. **ACCEPTED · MISCONFIG · confidence 55, informational** — CSP hardening is applied inconsistently across three HTML entry points serving one API origin (`/docs` hardened and CDN-pinned with SRI; `/v2/docs/openapi` reduced to `default-src 'self'`; `/` and `/v2/docs/changelog` unset). The weaker path is the one the root page advertises. **Honestly scoped:** the served content is public, unauthenticated API documentation with no state-changing action, so `frame-ancestors` absence yields no clickjackable target and this is explicitly *not* claimed as clickjacking — a rejected class in this program. It is recorded as a control-consistency defect and as evidence of a deployment-consistency gap in how the API origin ships security headers.
3. **ACCEPTED · METHOD · zero-request** — `operations_sorter.js` confirms the `x-sort-index` holes are UI sort slots. Closes the 2026-09-29 observation as definitively non-actionable.

## [REJECTED]
- **`/v2/room-types` as new surface** — unprobed for 36 cycles, but it declares no query parameters, so it adds nothing to the 9-operation binder map and returns the uniform `401/107B`. Recording it as measured, not as a finding.
- **YAML/3.0-twin as a finding** — re-diffed against the JSON; identical 38 paths, absent `securitySchemes`, absent top-level and per-op `security` in every rendering. Serialization-only difference, reconfirming 2026-09-29.
- **Further undocumented REST routes from the orphan-schema primitive** — the transitive diff leaves only the audit family, already accounted for by `/v2/audit-log`. Primitive exhausted for REST; parking it.
- **Static-asset enumeration** — `/footer.css`, `/design_tokens_light.css`, `/logo_alfaview_normal_black.svg`, `/docs/stoplight/*`, `/docs/favicon.ico`, `/icon_alfaview_production.svg`, `/styles.css` all `200` and all public, inert, and contain no secrets or endpoints. Recording the surface, claiming nothing.

## [RISK]
- **Top-3 remain `AUTH_HELPED` and unmeasured.** Every authorization claim in this program rests on contract shape, not behaviour, because the edge proxy returns a uniform `401` before any application code executes. Nothing this cycle changed that.
- **Self-retraction discipline held.** Three consecutive prior cycles retracted inference-from-absence errors. This cycle I nearly recorded the CSP asymmetry as clickjacking; the measured basis does not support that and it is downgraded above.
- **Discovery-path fragility.** Two of the six new facts (`operations_sorter.js`, `openapi-3.0.*`) were missed in 36 cycles purely because relative-path resolution and the root page's link set were never followed. The root page is the authoritative index and should be re-parsed whenever a delta cycle runs, not just `/v2/docs/openapi.json`.

## [NEXT]
One action: **request two credentials from the program — a self-owned account with 2FA enabled, and a company API key for the same account's tenant — then run the one differential that finding 1 requires and that nothing unauthenticated can substitute for:**

```
POST https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/password   {"companyId":…,"username":…,"password":…}  # expect 403 (2FA enforced)
POST https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/auth/api-key    {"clientId":…,"companyId":…,"key":…}       # expect 200 + accessToken (2FA skipped)
```

If the second returns a token while the first returns `403`, finding 1 is confirmed at full confidence and its impact class is established: a single leaked company API key yields a session for any 2FA-protected user in that tenant, with no signal in the response that the second factor was bypassed. This is the highest-value unblockable-by-recon item in the program and it converts the last AUTH-class claim that does not depend on an IDOR.
