[NEW] ACCEPTED INFO @ apis.alfaview.com: there are **two distinct permission schemas**, which the prior 38 cycles treated as one. `Permissions` (CreatePermissions body, `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions`) is a strict 9-boolean set with **all 9 in `required`** = atomic full replace, so a single call grants a complete permission set including `admin:true` and `promote:true` with no intermediate state. `PermissionsEdit` (`PATCH /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}`) is the all-optional partial delta. This makes the create route the more dangerous of the two write paths: one atomic full-admin grant versus an incremental delta, and it is the route whose target identifier is the unconstrained cross-namespace `participantId`.
[NEW] ACCEPTED INFO @ apis.alfaview.com GET /v2/permission-groups: confirmed as the enumeration source for the permission-group binding test. Returns an array of `PermissionGroup{id, name, permissions}`, all 3 required, where `permissions` is the full 9-boolean `Permissions` set and the `name` example is literally `"Admin"`. This route returns, in one call, every permission group's ID, name, and complete attached permission set — i.e. exactly the `{permissionGroupId}` value that `GuestLinkCreate` and `GroupLinkCreate` require the caller to supply. It is `roomList`-scoped at most (it declares no scope parameter), and it is the reason HYP 2 is now single-step rather than two-step.
