[HYP] CreatePermissions grants room-admin to any company-wide principal ID because participantId is an unconstrained, cross-namespace body identifier
class: IDOR
asset: apis.alfaview.com POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions
confidence: 80
reasoning: |
  - Path carries scope `roomId` (bare `type: string`).
  - Body uses `Permissions` (CreatePermissions) with **all 9 booleans required** = atomic full-permission set (including `admin`, `promote`).
  - `ParticipantPermissions.participantId` is bare `type: string`, documented as "user ID / guest link ID / group link ID to which the permissions apply" (three namespaces, one field, no discriminator, no `pattern`; contract contains zero `"uuid"` and zero `pattern` keys).
  - Target IDs obtainable company-wide via `GET /v2/guest-links` (un-narrowable list returning `accessKey`, `joinUrl`, `dialInCode`, `emailAddress`, `id`, `roomId`, `permissionGroupId`, `createdBy`).
  - `TokenUserPermissions` is a closed 7-boolean vocabulary with **no guest-link/group-link axis**; room-scoped siblings exist separately.
  - 422/88B `ACTION_INVALID` is a post-lookup business tier (not a format oracle) for synthetic values; 403 prose exists but contract has no declarative security scheme.
evidence_needed: |
  - With an authorized token for a self-owned low-privilege account and a room that account does not moderate: does CreatePermissions return `403` (closed) or `204` (BOLA/escalation)?
  - If `204`, confirm the permission set is actually applied (not transient). If `409`/other, record verbatim.
verify_steps: |
  1. `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/users/me/company` (Authorization: Bearer <token>) — obtain `companyId` (sole 200 supplier).
  2. `GET https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/guest-links?limit=1` (Authorization: Bearer <token>) — obtain one `id` (cross-namespace target). Alternatively use a known userId from `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/participants` in same tenant if available.
  3. Choose `roomId` in same tenant that token owner does **not** moderate.
  4. **ONE** `POST https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` (Authorization: Bearer <token>) with JSON body: {"participantId":"<id>","permissions":{"admin":true,"voice":true,"video":true,"promote":true,"join":true,"screen":true,"vip":true,"chat":true,"upload":true}}. Record status, `Content-Type`, body verbatim.
impact: |
  - If 204: low-privilege account grants itself `admin`+`promote` on any company room using an ID harvested from unscoped list (tenant-wide room takeover). 
  - If 403: closed; no direct impact.
testability: AUTH_HELPED

[HYP] Meeting-scoped bulk link creation binds caller-chosen permission group (out-of-scope group binding)
class: BUSLOGIC
asset: apis.alfaview.com POST /v2/meetings
confidence: 64
reasoning: |
  - `MeetingCreate.guestLinks` and `.groupLinks` require caller-supplied `permissionGroupId` (bare `type: string`), no documented constraint on which groups caller may bind.
  - `GET /v2/permission-groups` returns every group as `{id, name, permissions}` (full 9-bool `Permissions` set); `name` example `"Admin"`. Enumeration source exists.
  - Three issuance paths now mapped (room-scoped bulk, meeting-scoped bulk, unscoped PATCH) all accept caller-chosen `permissionGroupId`.
  - `TokenUserPermissions` has 7 booleans, **no permission-group axis**; no declared permission expresses "may bind this permission group".
evidence_needed: |
  - With authorized token: does `POST /v2/meetings` accept a `permissionGroupId` whose attached `permissions` include `admin` but which caller should not hold? Does it return 403/422, or 201 with joinUrl?
verify_steps: |
