**STEP 5 — NEXT ACTION**

[NEXT] HUMAN: Provide **one self-owned LOW-PRIVILEGE** alfaview account in a tenant you control, plus **one room** in that same tenant that the account **does not moderate**. Do **not** send any other data. With that single input I will (a) call `GET /v2/users/me/company` and `GET /v2/guest-links?limit=1` (read-only), (b) attempt **one** `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` against that non-moderated room with a harvested target `participantId` and atomic full permissions set (including `admin:true`, `promote:true`), and (c) record the exact status/body verbatim. This directly tests the 80-confidence CreatePermissions BOLA with minimal blast radius (self-owned tenant only). No cross-tenant tests.

**STEP 6 — LEARNING**

[LEARN] REJECTED IDOR @ apis.alfaview.com POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions: retracted earlier impact claim conflating `Permissions.admin` (CreatePermissions body) with `PermissionsEdit.admin` (PATCH route). Create path uses atomic `Permissions` with all 9 booleans required; documented `admin` meaning on Create is only "the associated user is an admin" — not the richer scope sentence from PATCH. HYP confidence corrected 82→80.

[LEARN] ACCEPTED INFO @ apis.alfaview.com: `Permissions` (CreatePermissions) vs `PermissionsEdit` (PATCH) are distinct schemas — Create is atomic full set, PATCH is partial delta. Create is the more dangerous write path given unconstrained `participantId`.

[LEARN] ACCEPTED INFO @ apis.alfaview.com GET `/v2/permission-groups`: returns every group `{id,name,permissions}` (full 9-bool set) including `admin` template; enumeration source for meeting-scoped `permissionGroupId` binding (enables single-step test).

[LEARN] REJECTED MISCONFIG @ apis.alfaview.com (documentation-only): contract declares no machine-readable auth requirements (top-level `security=null`, `securitySchemes` empty, `Authorization` present but never `required:true`, no per-op `security`); 2/57 ops omit even 401 prose. Auth state must be determined from wire behavior, not declarations.

[LEARN] NO_ANOMALY @ apis.alfaview.com POST `/v2/auth/*`: the 4 ops without `Authorization` header are exactly the 4 body-credential exchanges (`/auth/api-key`, `/auth/group-link`, `/auth/guest-link`, `/auth/password`); 403 patterns internally coherent.

[LEARN] PROCEDURAL: auditing prior output against spec caught a second fabrication (UUID-pattern claim; misattributed permission sentence). Contract text must be quoted only after per-field lookup.

**STEP 7 — RISK**

[RISK] alfaview gmbh: 66 (unchanged). No new unauthenticated surface exposure this cycle; strongest asset remains CreatePermissions BOLA at 80 (unconstrained cross-namespace `participantId`, atomic full-admin grant). Meeting-scoped permission-group binding at 64 is plausible but lower confidence. The introspect client-auth omission is structural but token-gated; device_authorize unregistered-client_id test is decisive either way (44). Four HIGH-value chains still converge on a single missing input: one self-owned low-privilege account + non-moderated room in same tenant. Mass assignment is closed across write surface; validation-before-auth is bounded to query-param routes (path params correctly 401). No claim of PII/config disclosure; all findings are authorization/logic flaws pending wire confirmation.
