Built the full path-param map. Unscoped routes use a generic `{id}`
(`/v2/rooms/{id}`, `/v2/users/{id}`, `/v2/guest-links/{id}`, `/v2/group-links/{id}`,
`/v2/meetings/{id}`); room-scoped routes use `{roomId}`; nested resources use
`{roomId}` + `{id}`/`{userId}`/`{subroomId}`.
Hypothesis was: an authorization layer keyed on the *named* param would leave
`PATCH/DELETE /v2/rooms/{id}` unbound. **Downgraded, not promoted** — Express, FastAPI
and Spring all bind path params by position, so the name is documentation only.
Recorded as refuted so it is not re-proposed.

### E. NEW — MISSING BRIDGE STEP IN THE CreatePermissions CHAIN
`GET /v2/rooms/{id}/participants` is the only operation that discloses *who* is in a room,
and it was **absent** from the previously documented 3-step chain. It is the step that
tells the tester *which* `participantId` to target. Corrected 4-step chain:
1. `GET /v2/rooms` -> company room ID set (self-visible)
2. `GET /v2/rooms/{id}/participants` -> victim principal IDs in target room
3. `GET /v2/guest-links?limit=1` -> harvest attacker-controlled `participantId`
4. `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` -> atomic grant incl. `admin`, `promote`
Still **contract-proven, zero wire evidence.** Confidence unchanged at 80.

### F. CONFIRMED — permission schema symmetry, no PATCH-only escalation field
`Permissions` (create) and `PermissionsEdit` (patch) expose the **identical 9 fields**
(`admin, chat, join, promote, screen, upload, video, vip, voice`); create is
non-nullable booleans, patch is nullable (partial update). `additionalProperties:false`
on both. Set difference PATCH-only = **none**; CREATE-only = **none**.
There is no hidden field reachable only through the PATCH verb.

### G. SHARPENED — the unscoped-mutation escalation primitive
`PATCH /v2/guest-links/{id}` is on an **unscoped** route yet its `GuestLinkUpdate` body
(9 fields) permits re-binding **`permissionGroupId`** (nullable) and extending
**`validUntil`** / flipping **`dialInAllowed`**. Note the schema *requires*
`displayName` + `sendEmail`, so the PATCH is effectively a near-full-replace that still
allows privilege re-pointing. `PATCH /v2/group-links/{id}` likewise allows
`permissionGroupId` re-binding. Escalation primitive for a stolen link ID, not standalone.

### H. LIVE GATE RE-CONFIRMED (read-only, <=1 rps, GET/HEAD only)
`GET /v2/rooms/{id}/participants`, `GET /v2/permission-groups`, `GET /v2/guest-links`
-> all **401**, all **107 bytes** (uniform -> no response-length oracle).
`HEAD /v2/rooms` -> 401. `GET /v2/docs/openapi.json` -> 200 `application/openapi+json`.

### STATE
Risk score **66**, unchanged. No new information-disclosure or auth-bypass class found.
The entire remaining high-value surface is still gated on one artifact: a self-owned
low-privilege bearer token.
