## DELTA THIS CYCLE
Live surface is **unchanged** (OpenAPI MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`, 38 paths / 57 ops; OIDC MD5 `f78a08fc`; all 8 standing probes returned byte-identical bodies). The new DELTA is **zero-request schema precision** that materially changes the top hypothesis.

### Correction that matters
My prior notes said the CreatePermissions body is `Permissions`. **That was wrong.**

```
POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions
  body = ParticipantPermissions { participantId, permissions }
            └─ permissions = Permissions (all 9 booleans REQUIRED)
```

- `Permissions` is *not* referenced by any path; it is reached via `ParticipantPermissions`, `PermissionGroup`, `Room`, `RoomCreate`, `RoomUpdate`.
- `PermissionsEdit` (nullable fields) belongs **only** to `PATCH /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions/{userId}`.
- **`ParticipantPermissions.participantId`**: *"The user ID / guest link ID / group link ID to which the permissions apply."*

[FINAL] This is the vendor's own documentation confirming the principal selector is **polymorphic across three namespaces**, while the only scope binding is the unvalidated `roomId` path parameter. It converts the CreatePermissions BOLA from inference to vendor-confirmed design. `Permissions.admin` remains an unconditional *"If true, the associated user is an admin."* with no schema-level precondition.

[LEARN] Response codes give a **4-way discriminator** for the authorized test: `204`=escalation succeeded, `403`=correctly blocked, `409`=permission row already exists, `422`=ID invalid or precondition unmet. The verify test can no longer produce ambiguous results. `409` also implies an existence oracle over arbitrary principal×room pairs — currently unreachable (401 gate), so not reportable alone.

[HYP]
- `target`: api
- `hypothesis_id`: apis-001-create-permissions-bola
- `title`: `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` accepts a company-wide guest-link/group-link ID as `participantId` and grants atomic room-admin rights in a room the caller does not moderate
- `confidence`: 82
- `impact`: A low-privileged company member holding `roomList`+guest-link read can mint a self-chosen principal and grant it `admin` in any company room, yielding room takeover, guest management, feature and file-share settings control.
- `evidence`: `ParticipantPermissions.participantId` documented as "user ID / guest link ID / group link ID" in one unconstrained string; `Permissions` requires all 9 booleans including unconditional `admin`; scope exists only as `roomId` path param (type string, no format/pattern); `GET /v2/guest-links` and `/v2/group-links` bind only `pageToken`+`limit`, exposing candidate IDs company-wide; `GET /v2/users/me/company` supplies `companyId`.
- `verification`: From one self-owned low-privilege token: `GET /v2/users/me/company` → `GET /v2/guest-links?limit=1` → exactly one authorized test-tenant POST to `/v2/rooms/{non-moderatedRoomId}/permissions` with `{"participantId":"<own guest-link id>","permissions":{"admin":true,"voice":true,"video":true,"promote":true,"join":true,"screen":true,"vip":true,"chat":true,"upload":true}}` → record verbatim status. `204` confirms BOLA; `403` falsifies.
