- `/v2/users/me/company` is the 38th OpenAPI path and sole 200-response supplier of `companyId`; `/v2/audit-log` is a live undocumented 39th path.
- Retracted premise: OpenAPI does not confirm UUID formats—`uuid` and `pattern` occur zero times; path parameters are unconstrained `type: string`.
- Retracted claim: `Permissions.admin` does not contain the PATCH scope text; that text belongs to `PermissionsEdit.admin`. `Permissions` (CREATE) is an atomic nine-boolean write.
- `GET /v2/guest-links` and `/v2/group-links` are company-wide, accept no measured `roomId`/`companyId` filters, and return credential-bearing data; authorization behavior remains untested.
- OAuth introspection accepts fabricated client IDs on POST-body and HTTP Basic for inactive tokens, but impact requires a valid token. `/oauth2/userinfo` correctly rejects forged JOSE tokens.
- Signup is anonymous but finish-signup is email-gated; obtaining a legitimate bearer is `HUMAN_ONLY`.
- Validation-before-auth affects documented query parameters on 9/26 GET operations, plus undocumented `/v2/audit-log`; it reproduces public schema and is informational, not a standalone high-severity finding.
- Tools `/whiteboard/` and poll RPC mappings are inventory facts only; no exploit has been demonstrated.

## Work State
### Completed
- Verified prod/beta OpenAPI parity at MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`.
- Identified `/v2/users/me/company`; it enables an authorized tester to obtain `companyId` through `GET /v2/users/me/company`.
- Mapped CreatePermissions as a contract-proven BOLA hypothesis: `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` with polymorphic body `participantId`, atomic `Permissions`, `admin:true`, `promote:true`.
- Measured that company-wide guest-link IDs can supply the CreatePermissions target; room membership/authorization binding remains untested.
- Closed API JWT confusion, guest-link validity oracle, SSRF, profile mass assignment, logout redirect, and undocumented plural invitation route as standalone findings.
- Established OAuth introspection client-auth omission as a same-deployment control failure; confidence `94`, pending valid-token confirmation.
- Determined `sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/device_authorize` is parked because its proposed confirmation requires a form POST outside passive GET/HEAD/OPTIONS probing.

### Active
- IDOR `80`: `apis.alfaview.com POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` may grant room-admin to an arbitrary same-company principal not moderating the target room.
- BUSLOGIC `64`: `apis.alfaview.com POST /v2/meetings` may bind caller-selected high-privilege `permissionGroupId` values to guest/group links.
- AUTH `94`: `sso.alfaview.com/oauth2/introspect` may expose valid-token metadata without verifying client credentials.
- Supporting lead: public `app.alfaview.com` bundle exposes `adminSwitchCompany` and tenant identifiers, but anonymous reachability and authorization behavior remain unmeasured.

### Blocked
- No self-owned low-privilege alfaview account, legitimate bearer token, or same-tenant non-moderated room is available.
- Signup completion requires an emailed activation token, so token-dependent tests cannot proceed anonymously.
- No valid token means introspection bypass impact remains conditional and cannot be reported as fully proven.

## Next Move
1. `[NEXT] HUMAN`: Obtain one self-owned low-privilege account in a controlled tenant and one room in that tenant the account does not moderate.
2. With authorization, run `GET /v2/users/me/company` and `GET /v2/guest-links?limit=1`, then perform exactly one minimal CreatePermissions test against the non-moderated room and record status, headers, and body verbatim; separately test introspection twice using the legitimate token.

