Cycle complete. Here's the 8-step output.

## 1. Executive Summary
No new reportable finding this cycle. I mapped two previously unexamined surfaces (the `app.alfaview.com/graphql` backend and `tools.alfaview.com/poll/pollservice`) and confirmed both correctly gate every business operation behind authentication. Spec parity is unchanged, so the standing two hypotheses remain the only reportable candidates — and both are still blocked on a self-owned account.

## 2. Surface Delta
Newly probed this cycle:
- `app.alfaview.com/graphql` — Apollo Server 4. Introspection disabled (`INTROSPECTION_DISABLED`), operation batching disabled, aliases do not bypass introspection filtering. `dev.alfaview.com` and `appstats.alfaview.com` do not resolve/serve; `staging.alfaview.com/graphql` and `beta-app.alfaview.com/graphql` return nginx 401.
- `tools.alfaview.com` — "Tools UI" SPA; backend is a gRPC-gateway at `/poll/pollservice/{list,get,create,delete,vote,hasVoted}` authenticating via `Grpc-Metadata-alfaview.token` (base64url→base64).

## 3. Authentication Testing
- GraphQL: 20+ field probes (`listAuthData`, `listRooms`, `searchCompanies`, `listCompaniesById`, `listAllUserIds`, `listUnverifiedAccounts`, `listAllUserProfiles`, `getPasscode`, `listAuditEvents`, `getFinishSignupLinkAsAdmin`, `createMagicToken`, `adminSwitchCompany`) all returned `UNAUTHENTICATED / "Missing access token"`. `adminTokenAuthenticate` requires a `refreshToken` cookie and returns `FORBIDDEN / "access denied"` when fabricated.
- Pollservice: all six verbs return uniform `403` gRPC `AUTHENTICATION_ERROR` regardless of `Authorization: Bearer`, `Grpc-Metadata-alfaview.token` value (absent, empty, `none`, 32×`0`, base64), or `Origin`. No token-format oracle.
- `apis.alfaview.com`: `/v2/users/me`, `/v2/users/me/company`, `/v2/guest-links`, `/v2/audit-log` all 401 unauthenticated. `/v2/auth/guest-link` returns identical `422 ACTION_INVALID` across three distinct access-key shapes — no validity oracle.

## 4. Authorization Testing
Not testable. Authorization requires two principals in one tenant (attacker + victim) and none are available. The `CreatePermissions` BOLA and meeting `permissionGroupId` hypotheses remain contract-level only.

## 5. Business Logic Testing
Not testable. Both business-logic candidates are authenticated-write paths gated by the missing account.

## 6. Technical Observations (low value, not reportable)
- GraphQL validation errors disclose reply type names and argument signatures (`Cannot query field "a" on type "ListAuditEventsReply"`). This is schema-shape only, no data. Program excludes descriptive error messages.
- `sso.alfaview.com/.well-known/openid-configuration` returns `issuer: "acme.com"` — an unconfigured template default. Informational only.
- `token` endpoint returns `not_licensed` for `client_credentials` (FusionAuth unlicensed feature) — dead end, correctly denied.
- JWKS at `/.well-known/jwks.json`: 7 keys, all RSA/RS256/`sig`. No `HS*` or `none` algorithm key, so classic algorithm-confusion is not applicable. `token_endpoint_auth_methods_supported` includes `none` (expected for public SPA PKCE).
- `/v2/audit-log` is confirmed undocumented but live: pre-auth query validation (422 for missing/malformed `from`/`to`) then 401. Reproduces public spec behavior.
- No CORS headers on `apis.alfaview.com`; `OPTIONS` returns 405.

## 7. Spec Parity
`https://apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json` and `https://beta-apis.alfaview.com/v2/docs/openapi.json` both 200, 132100B, MD5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`, 38 paths / 57 operations. Byte-identical. Note `beta.apis.alfaview.com` does not resolve; `beta-apis` is correct. Both snapshots saved to `recon-notes/openapi-2026-10-05.json` and `openapi-beta-2026-10-05.json`. `components.securitySchemes` and root `security` remain absent — every operation declares its own `Authorization` header parameter instead, which is why pre-auth validation surfaces before the 401.

## 8. Recommendations & Next Steps
1. `[NEXT]` Human: supply one self-owned low-privilege account in a controlled tenant plus one room in that tenant the account does not moderate. Everything else is blocked on this.
2. With access: `GET /v2/users/me/company` → `GET /v2/guest-links?limit=1` → exactly one `POST /v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` with `{"participantId":"<non-moderating guest link ID>","permissions":{"admin":true,"promote":true,"join":true,"voice":false,"video":false,"screen":false,"vip":false,"chat":false,"upload":false}}`. Record status, headers, and body verbatim. Expect 204 for a real BOLA, 403 if authorization is correct — that single response decides whether an80-confidence hypothesis is real.
3. Separately, introspect the legitimate token twice (`/oauth2/introspect` with and without correct client credentials) to settle the 94-confidence introspection finding.

## 9. Confidence Summary
| Item | Confidence | Blocker |
|---|---|---|
| CreatePermissions BOLA | 80 (unchanged) | needs 2 principals |
| Meeting permissionGroupId | 64 (unchanged) | needs account |
| Introspection client-auth | 94 (unchanged) | needs valid token |
| Unauthenticated GraphQL/poll disclosure | 3 (retired) | disproved this cycle |

No new standing delta beyond the two newly mapped, properly gated surfaces.
