- Run the 8-step bug-bounty analyst loop for the alfaview gmbh program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), producing only structured [HYP]/[PRIO]/[PARKED]/[FINAL]/[NEXT]/[LEARN]/[RISK] blocks each cycle.
- Current phase: POC against target "api"; all HIGH-value chains are AUTH_HELPED/HUMAN_ONLY pending one human-supplied low-privilege account + room + opaque access token.

## Important Details
- Scope: ONLY assets from scope.yml + inventory/alfaview.md — company-owned infrastructure, web/desktop/mobile apps, APIs, backend, support systems, portals, websites, domains including alfaview.com and company subdomains.
- Probe rules: passive-first, ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only for live probes; no auth-bypass/mutating tests against live customer data; no POST unless explicitly justified; facts vs hypotheses strictly separated; sha256 any secret; every claim must trace to context or own read-only probe.
- OUT OF SCOPE classes (long list) include: brute-force/rate-limit/lockout, username enumeration, descriptive-errors-only, robots.txt, clickjacking w/o exploit, TLS best practice, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, public login panels, known-vuln libraries without program-specific exploit, exposure of customer/employee/financial/auth data during testing.
- Key standing facts:
  - OpenAPI: md5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`, 132100B, 38 paths, 57 ops, byte-identical on beta-apis.alfaview.com; YAML twin md5 `6738669c`; `components.securitySchemes` absent, top-level `security` absent. Undocumented live 39th path: `GET /v2/audit-log`.
