## Objective
- Act as senior bug bounty analyst for the alfaview gmbh program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step cycle (DELTA → PRIORITIZE → HYPOTHESES → SELF-CRITIQUE → NEXT → LEARNING → RISK) over an accumulated knowledge base, inventory, and ranked leads.
- Deep-hunt high-value classes (IDOR/BOLA, broken auth, OAuth flaws, mass assignment, SSRF, GraphQL) with strict passive-first, read-only discipline; separate facts from hypotheses.

## Important Details
- Scope ONLY: alfaview.com and company-operated subdomains per scope.yml + inventory/alfaview.md.
- Live probe rules: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps (~1.1s sleeps), no POST/mutating calls, no auth-bypass attempts, no customer data touched, secrets recorded as md5 only, guessed URLs never become findings (require a second method, e.g. DNS getent vs HTTP, before accepting deltas).
- Out-of-scope (REJECTED) classes enumerated in prompt: brute-force/rate-limit, descriptive errors only, username enumeration, clickjack w/o exploit, TLS best practice, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, etc.
- Standing retractions that must not regress: "OpenAPI confirms path-param UUID patterns" is FALSE (zero `uuid`/`pattern` keys); `Permissions.admin` scope sentence misattributed (lives on `PermissionsEdit.admin`); no accessKey existence oracle (two-tier taxonomy: schema 422 / business 422/88B ACTION_INVALID); pre-auth query-binder oracle rejected as standalone (reproduces public spec only); 403-declaration asymmetry not load-bearing standalone; JWT alg-confusion closed (apis + sso `/oauth2/userinfo`); logout open redirect closed; SSRF closed on REST; mass assignment closed (21/21 body schemas `additionalProperties:false`); GraphQL anonymous exposure retired; device_authorize unregistered-client claim retracted (401 invalid_client_id).
- Current OpenAPI: 174787B, md5 `06231fadca0b36c314476322337976db`, 38 paths/57 ops/69 schemas, first-ever `components.securitySchemes.accessToken` (`bearerFormat: opaque`, description says token "accepted without the 'Bearer ' prefix"), per-op `security` on 53/57 ops; rotation 2026-10-06 (first since 2026-09-28, prior md5 `284a3383c1ac3cfc9152ffcc631891f2`).
- Dated snapshot stored: `recon-notes/alfaview-openapi-2026-10-06.json`; older baseline `recon-notes/alfaview-openapi.yaml` (37 paths, predates two rotations).
- GraphQL endpoint exists ONLY on app.alfaview.com (apis `/v2/graphql` = 404 edge-proxy catch — never probe). Bare-GET graphql 400 must not be compared with header-qualified (`x-apollo-operation-name` / `apollo-require-preflight`) `__typename` 200; always state header set.
- SSO standing facts: OIDC md5 `f78a08fc`/2169B (issuer=`acme.com`, `introspection_endpoint` absent while `/oauth2/introspect` live at OPTIONS 405, advertises DPoP+device_code+password+client_credentials), JWKS md5 `3f8d456c`/16257B at `/.well-known/jwks.json` (7×RS256; oscillates 200↔404; `/oauth2/jwks` = 404).
- Introspect bypass refined: client auth enforced ONLY for JWT-shaped tokens (3 segments, seg2 = base64 JSON); opaque tokens → 200 `{"active":false}` with fabricated client_id on POST-body and Basic; alfaview tokens are opaque base64, so bypass applies to issued tokens.
- Diagnostics host fact: client-diagnostics-ingest.alfaview.com is NOT NXDOMAIN — /health 200/16B md5 `3a0386dd`, / 404/39B md5 `d18415bd`, uniform 404 across 6 paths + OPTIONS; retire NXDOMAIN line everywhere.
- Discipline this cycle: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps, no POST, no auth-bypass, guessed URLs (6 on diag host) used only for surface mapping.

