## Objective
- Act as senior bug bounty analyst for the alfaview gmbh program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a 7-step structured analysis cycle (DELTA → PRIORITIZE → HYPOTHESES → SELF-CRITIQUE → NEXT → LEARNING → RISK) over an accumulating knowledge base, using only passive read-only probes (GET/HEAD/OPTIONS, ≤1 rps).

## Important Details
- Scope: only alfaview-owned infrastructure per scope.yml + inventory/alfaview.md (alfaview.com and company subdomains). Out-of-scope REJECTED classes include brute-force/rate-limit, descriptive errors only, username enumeration, clickjacking w/o exploit, OPTIONS/TRACE as findings, etc.
- Probe rules: passive-first, ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, no auth-bypass/mutating tests, no customer data, secrets recorded as md5 only, guessed URLs never become findings (verify canonical URLs from inventory/alfaview.md first).
- Standing procedural rules learned: quote contract text only after per-field lookup (two prior fabrications caught); state header set when comparing graphql 400 vs 200 (header-keyed CSRF guard: `x-apollo-operation-name` / `apollo-require-preflight` flip GET `query={__typename}` 400→200 md5 c2b4dd58); never probe apis.alfaview.com for /graphql (404 catch — GraphQL exists only on app.alfaview.com); delta claims need 2 methods (DNS getent + HTTP); bare-GET graphql 400 must not be conflated with apis host 404.
- Current standing fingerprints: OpenAPI 200/127532B (older hash) vs rotated 174787B md5 `06231fadca0b36c314476322337976db` (38 paths/57 ops/69 schemas, first-ever `components.securitySchemes.accessToken` with `bearerFormat: opaque`, per-op security on 53/57); OIDC md5 `f78a08fc`/2169B (issuer=acme.com, `introspection_endpoint` absent while /oauth2/introspect live OPTIONS 405); JWKS md5 `3f8d456c`/16257B (7×RS256); users/me 401/107B md5 `60ed2f29` + `www-authenticate: Bearer`; audit-log 422/232B; graphql GET 400/406B (app host); tools poll list 501/55B; tools /whiteboard/ OPTIONS 404/47B; client-diagnostics-ingest /health 200/16B md5 `3a0386dd` (NOT NXDOMAIN — that fact retired).
- Key standing findings: introspect client-auth bypass conf 92-94 (conditional: enforced only for JWT-shaped tokens; alfaview tokens are opaque base64 → applies to real tokens), HUMAN_ONLY; CreatePermissions BOLA conf 80 AUTH_HELPED; 403-declaration asymmetry conf 58 rejected standalone; meeting-scoped bulk link issuance 64; diagnostics-ingest H-90 conf 25 PARKED.
- Standing retractions (must be preserved): "OpenAPI confirms path-param UUID patterns" FALSE (zero `uuid`/`pattern` in doc); Permissions.admin scope sentence misattributed (lives on PermissionsEdit.admin/PATCH); no accessKey existence oracle (2-tier: schema 422, business 422/88B ACTION_INVALID); query-binder oracle reproduces public spec only; JWT alg-confusion closed (apis + sso userinfo); logout open redirect closed; SSRF closed on REST; mass assignment closed (21/21 body schemas additionalProperties:false); GraphQL anonymous exposure retired; device_authorize unregistered client_id claim retracted (401 invalid_client_id).
- All HIGH chains are HUMAN-gated: need one self-owned low-priv account + opaque token from legitimate signup (email-gated).
- Passive surface at 40+ cycle plateau; E[findings] from further unauthenticated probing ≈ 0.

## Work State
### Completed
- 40+ analysis cycles run; full 55-host inventory probed; extensive contract-level analysis of apis.alfaview.com OpenAPI (two rotations: 37→38 paths, then 174787B auth-scheme depth).
- Pre-auth validation map complete: 10/26 GET ops validate query params pre-auth (binder is per-operation, negative-controlled); path params validate post-auth.
- Mapped: 4 credential-exchange endpoints (/v2/auth/{password, guest-link, group-link, api-key}), /v2/users/me/company (GetOwnCompany, sole companyId supplier), live undocumented /v2/audit-log (39th path), tools poll + second /whiteboard/ RPC mount, support WordPress map, whiteboard.alfaview.com structural map.
- 2026-10-06 OpenAPI rotation attributed (declaration-depth only, no path moved); dated snapshot stored at `recon-notes/alfaview-openapi-2026-10-06.json`.
- Latest cycle 2026-10-07 09:28 emitted only a LEARN (NO_DELTA on standing probes).

### Active
- Standing lead set: introspect bypass 94 (top ranked, from art/lead_nemotron3.txt), CreatePermissions BOLA 80, 403 asymmetry 58, H-90 diagnostics 25.
- New-ish lead H-91: `production-*` hosts are deploy mirrors of documented hosts (webclient/app/equipment), staging-support Basic-gated — close as NO_DELTA-to-findings.
- Program RISK last recorded at 88/100 (one earlier reading 62/100); discipled probes all read-only.

### Blocked
- All 3 HIGH hypotheses blocked on HUMAN_ONLY step: one self-owned low-priv alfaview account, one non-moderated room, one opaque access token (plus optional expired token) from a legitimate self-owned signup.
- Passive plateau: no new rotation or hostname means no new passive increment; CT diff capped at once per 12h.

## Next Move
1. [NEXT] HUMAN: unchanged request — one session, one owned mailbox — execute unauthenticated signup at app.alfaview.com/graphql (mutation Signup → email → FinishSignup) to obtain a valid bearer token.
2. Then with token, ≤1 rps wire probes: (a) GET `/v2/users/me/company` + GET `/v2/group-links?limit=1`; (b) exactly one POST `/v2/rooms/{roomId}/permissions` (BOLA check → 204/403/409/422 discriminator); (c) three POSTs to sso `/oauth2/introspect` (POST-body, Basic, refresh hint) with fabricated client_id; (d) GET `/v2/auth/token-info` live vs expired token.

