## Objective
- Act as senior bug bounty analyst for the alfaview gmbh program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a fixed 8-step analysis cycle over a growing knowledge base of passive-recon findings to surface real, in-scope vulnerabilities.
- Currently in POC phase targeting `api`; produce only structured blocks ([DELTA]/[PRIO]/[HYP]/[PARKED]/[FINAL]/[NEXT]/[LEARN]/[RISK]) each cycle, passive-first.

## Important Details
- Scope ONLY: company-owned infrastructure, alfaview web/desktop/mobile apps, APIs, backends, support systems, portals, websites, domains incl. alfaview.com and company-operated subdomains.
- Rejected classes (never report): DoS/lockout, descriptive errors/headers, robots.txt, outdated libs, OPTIONS/TRACE, logout CSRF, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, self-XSS, username enumeration, brute-force/rate-limit, TLS best practice, clickjacking w/o exploit, mail config, known-vuln libs w/o POC, password/recovery policy, public login panels, lack of email verification, and any exposure of customer/employee/financial/auth data during testing.
- Probe rules: passive-first, ≤1 rps, GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only for live probes; no auth-bypass/mutating tests; no POST without human authorization; guessed URLs never become findings; delta claims require two methods (e.g., DNS getent + HTTP); secrets recorded as md5 only; standing-probe lines must carry BOTH size and md5; always state the full header set when comparing responses.
- Contract claims must be quoted only after per-field lookup — two prior fabrications caught: (1) "OpenAPI spec confirms path-param UUID patterns" is FALSE (live doc contains "uuid" zero times, zero `pattern` keys); (2) `Permissions.admin` scope sentence misattributed — it lives on `PermissionsEdit.admin` (PATCH), not `Permissions` (CREATE).
- Canonical URLs: recover from `inventory/alfaview.md:1096` and `leads/lead-bigpickle.md` verify_steps; never probe `apis.alfaview.com/v2/graphql` (404 — GraphQL exists only on `app.alfaview.com`).
- Current standing hashes: OpenAPI JSON md5 `06231fadca0b36c314476322337976db` (174787B, 38 paths, 57 ops, first-ever `components.securitySchemes.accessToken` with `bearerFormat: opaque`, per-op `security` on 53/57 ops; rotated 2026-10-06 from `284a3383`); OIDC md5 `f78a08fc` (2169B, issuer=acme.com, introspection_endpoint absent); JWKS md5 `3f8d456c` (16257B, 7×RS256, path `/.well-known/jwks.json`); users/me 401/107B md5 `60ed2f29` + `www-authenticate: Bearer`; audit-log 422/232B; graphql GET 400/406B (flips to 200/32B `c2b4dd58` with `x-apollo-operation-name` or `apollo-require-preflight` header); tools poll list 501/55B; tools `/whiteboard/` 404/47B; client-diagnostics-ingest /health 200/16B md5 `3a0386dd` (NOT NXDOMAIN — retire that fact).
- Dated snapshot for future rotation attribution: `recon-notes/alfaview-openapi-2026-10-06.json`; pre-rotation baseline `recon-notes/alfaview-openapi.yaml` (37 paths, predates two rotations).
- CT diff capped at once per 12h (last ran 09:28, next eligible ~21:28 UTC).

