## Objective
- Act as senior bug bounty analyst for the alfaview gmbh program (report channel: bugs.olivermaicher.eu), running a fixed 8-step analysis cycle (DELTA→PRIORITIZE→HYPOTHESES→SELF-CRITIQUE→NEXT→LEARNING→RISK) over passive reconnaissance of in-scope alfaview assets.
- Advance the top-3 hypotheses toward proof while respecting read-only constraints; all HIGH-value chains are currently blocked on obtaining a self-owned credential (HUMAN-gated).

## Important Details
- Scope: ONLY company-owned infrastructure, web/desktop/mobile apps, APIs, backend/support systems, customer portals, domains operated by alfaview gmbh (alfaview.com + subdomains), per scope.yml + inventory/alfaview.md.
- Probe discipline: passive-first, ≤1 rps (1.1–1.5s sleeps), GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, no POST/mutating calls, no auth-bypass attempts, no customer data, secrets recorded as md5 only, guessed URLs never promoted to findings, every standing-probe line must carry size AND md5, delta claims require 2 methods (DNS getent + HTTP).
- REJECTED classes (do not re-raise): descriptive errors only, brute-force/rate-limit, username enumeration, clickjacking w/o exploit, OPTIONS/TRACE standalone, robots.txt, etc. (full list in prompt).
- Standing retractions to preserve: UUID path-param patterns claim FALSE (zero "uuid"/"pattern" in spec); Permissions.admin scope sentence misattributed (lives on PermissionsEdit.admin for PATCH, HYP corrected 82→80); no accessKey existence oracle (422/88B ACTION_INVALID two-tier only); query-binder oracle reproduces public spec only (rejected standalone); 403-declaration asymmetry not behaviorally load-bearing standalone; JWT alg-confusion closed (apis opaque tokens + sso userinfo, all forgeries → access_token_failed_processing); logout open redirect closed (302→/); SSRF closed on REST (no URL-typed request params); mass assignment closed (21/21 body schemas additionalProperties:false); GraphQL anonymous exposure retired; device_authorize unregistered-client claim retracted (401 invalid_client_id); graphql exists ONLY on app.alfaview.com (apis /v2/graphql = 404 catch, never probe).
- Current baselines: OpenAPI JSON 174787B md5 `06231fadca0b36c314476322337976db` (38 paths, 57 ops, first-ever `components.securitySchemes.accessToken` bearerFormat opaque + per-op security on 53/57; YAML twin 2283xxB, parity proven), prod=beta byte-identical; snapshot stored at recon-notes/alfaview-openapi-2026-10-06.json. sso OIDC 200/2169B md5 `f78a08fc` (issuer=acme.com, introspection_endpoint absent while /oauth2/introspect live OPTIONS 405), JWKS 200/16257B md5 `3f8d456c` (7×RS256); users/me 401/107B md5 `60ed2f29` + www-authenticate: Bearer; app graphql GET bare 400/406B but header `x-apollo-operation-name`/`apollo-require-preflight` flips `query={__typename}` to 200/32B md5 `c2b4dd58`; tools poll list 501/55B, /whiteboard/ 404/47B, /health/ 200/615B; client-diagnostics-ingest /health 200/16B md5 `3a0386dd` (NXDOMAIN fact retired).
- Ranked hypotheses (2026-10-07 21:35): [94] sso introspect bypass (from art/lead_nemotron3.txt); [92] introspect client-auth (HUMAN_ONLY); [80] CreatePermissions BOLA; [58] 403-declaration asymmetry (DECLARATION-ONLY); H-90 diagnostics-ingest write (25, PARKED); H-88/H-89 open.
- Introspect bypass is CONDITIONAL: client auth enforced only for JWT-shaped tokens (3 segments, seg2 = base64 JSON); alfaview tokens are opaque base64 → bypass applies to the product's own token type.
- Signup mutation (app.alfaview.com/graphql, from public bundles) is the sole unauthenticated path to a legit bearer token — email-gated, HUMAN_ONLY; gates all HIGH chains (introspect 92, IDOR/BOLA 80).
- Risk score: 88/100 (prior entry said 62 then 88; latest [RISK] = 88/100 flat); passive plateau 42+ cycles; E[findings] from unauth probing ≈0; risk is stall, not miss.
- CT diff capped at once per 12h (last run 09:28, next ~21:28 UTC).
