6438:reasoning: The mount is real and pre-auth (47B gRPC status envelope on /whiteboard/**, while /health/, /foo/ return the 615B SPA catch-all and /poll/ returns Go-native 19B). But the discriminator that would make it actionable is absent: the mount returns code:5 (NOT_FOUND) flat, whereas the poll gateway returns code:12 (UNIMPLEMENTED) on a wrong method. Three path shapes — empty, canonical gRPC service/method, and a nonsense control — are byte-identical, so the verb set is not recoverable without a client that speaks gRPC-web. Zero whiteboard references exist in the 137343B public bundle, so no client asset reveals it either.
