6198:reasoning: Proven this cycle by controlled differential, not inference from a single 404. With `Ga=${origin}/poll/pollservice` pinned in the public bundle, the host's gateway convention is `/<prefix>/<service>`. Against that convention `/whiteboard/` returns `{"code": 5, "message": "Not Found", "details":[]}` (47B, application/json) while the negative controls `/health/`, `/foo/`, `/zzznotreal/` all return the 615B SPA shell and `/poll/` returns a Go-native `404 page not found` (19B, text/plain, nosniff). The `/whiteboard/` envelope additionally uses a different marshaller than the poll gateway's 45B compact jsonpb, so it is a separate server implementation. The 47B response carries no `WWW-Authenticate` and no 401 on any probed path, i.e. the router is reachable pre-authentication. The bundle contains no `whiteboard` string, so no client contract exists to compare against. `whiteboard.alfaview.com` does not expose this mount, so the renderer host and the data RPC are distinct systems.
