- Passive-first, read-only reconnaissance and hypothesis prioritization; all high-value chains remain HUMAN-gated pending a self-owned account/token.

## Important Details
- Phase/target: `{"phase": "POC", "target": "api"}`.
- In-scope: only company-owned alfaview infrastructure (alfaview.com + subdomains), per scope.yml + inventory/alfaview.md. Report channel bugs.olivermaicher.eu.
- Probe rules: GET/HEAD/OPTIONS only, ≤1 rps (~1.1–1.5s sleeps), no POST/mutating calls, no auth-bypass attempts, no customer data, secrets recorded as md5 only, guessed URLs never promoted to findings, every delta claim requires a second method (DNS `getent` + HTTP), every standing-probe line must carry size AND md5 together.
- REJECTED classes (must not be re-reported): brute-force/rate-limit, descriptive errors, JWT alg-confusion (apis + sso userinfo), logout open redirect, SSRF on REST, mass assignment (21/21 body schemas `additionalProperties:false`), GraphQL anonymous exposure (43/45 roots auth-gated), username enumeration, cookie flags on non-sensitive data, clickjacking w/o exploit, OPTIONS/TRACE standalone.
- Standing retractions to preserve: "OpenAPI confirms path-param UUID patterns" FALSE (zero `uuid`/`pattern` in live doc); Permissions.admin scope sentence misattributed (lives on PermissionsEdit.admin/PATCH); no accessKey existence oracle; pre-auth query-binder oracle reproduces public spec only (informational); 403-declaration asymmetry not load-bearing standalone; introspect device_authorize claim retracted (401 invalid_client_id).
